{"id": "7a91b8ae-ea85-547f-a078-af9f78eaf950", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Contracts", "question": "What makes an agreement a valid contract under Bangladeshi law?", "key_points": ["The Contract Act 1872 sets the test", "Free consent of parties who are competent to contract", "A lawful consideration and a lawful object", "Not declared void by law; applies the test to the facts"], "source_url": "https://bdlaws.minlaw.gov.bd/act-26.html", "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "49e6a8af-7b55-553a-8a15-51887ee48139", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Drafting", "question": "What are the main parts of a legal notice?", "key_points": ["Sender, recipient, date and the advocate's details", "Clear facts and the legal basis of the claim", "What the recipient must do, and by when", "Polite, precise language, with a copy kept on file"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "36e9d236-a4c3-5ce5-989c-0787c5b92834", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Court procedure", "question": "What is the difference between a civil case and a criminal case?", "key_points": ["Civil: a private dispute, such as property or a contract, for a remedy", "Criminal: an offence against the state, which can lead to punishment", "Different courts, procedure and standard of proof", "The same facts can sometimes lead to both"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "44411d27-84e3-527a-87e3-fdf2aa7d20d0", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Legal career", "question": "How does a law graduate become an advocate in Bangladesh?", "key_points": ["Enrolment is through the Bangladesh Bar Council", "A period of pupillage with a senior advocate comes first", "The enrolment exam has stages: MCQ, written and viva", "Check the Bar Council's current notices for rules and dates"], "source_url": "https://www.barcouncil.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "dbdb0607-90a7-5bf1-9c0e-d9ce838e5d02", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Company law", "question": "A client wants to form a private limited company. What are the main steps?", "key_points": ["Clear the company name with RJSC", "Prepare the memorandum and articles of association", "Register online with RJSC and pay the fees", "Then: trade licence, tax registration and a bank account"], "source_url": "https://roc.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "f7e3b3e8-240f-5fa5-912f-80dc02ef3134", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Company law", "question": "What must a company file with RJSC each year, and what happens if it does not?", "key_points": ["An annual return after the annual general meeting, with directors and shareholders", "Separate forms when things change, such as new directors or share transfers", "Late or missing filings can bring fines", "Keep a filing calendar and check the Companies Act 1994 and RJSC notices"], "source_url": "https://bdlaws.minlaw.gov.bd/act-788.html", "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "638844ce-143f-5ead-8830-5d6481ecb405", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Contracts", "question": "A client gives you a supply contract to review in one day. What do you check first?", "key_points": ["Parties, scope, price, payment and delivery terms", "Who carries the risk: liability, penalties, force majeure", "How it ends and how disputes are settled: court or arbitration", "Marks the risky clauses and suggests plain wording"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "edc3d8f4-90c8-5494-af03-3a79f372be66", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Drafting", "question": "A client wants the agreement in Bangla, but your draft is in English. How do you handle drafting in two languages?", "key_points": ["Agrees which language controls if the two versions differ", "Translates the legal meaning, not word for word", "Keeps defined terms the same throughout", "Has a second person check both versions"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "a1d8e8d3-6fee-5537-abc1-90b579345d8f", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Client communication", "question": "How do you explain a legal risk to a client who is not a lawyer?", "key_points": ["Plain words, without Latin or jargon", "What could happen, how likely it is, and what it would cost", "Options, and your recommendation", "Confirms the advice in a short email"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "5bf62092-43fc-5e8f-9ace-8e2dd5434a3d", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Ethics", "question": "A friend asks you about a case your firm is handling for another client. What do you say?", "key_points": ["Says nothing about the case: client matters are confidential", "Polite but firm, without confirming even small details", "Tells the senior lawyer if the person keeps asking"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "a4950440-e6e7-5764-88f1-9002a84f8092", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Court procedure", "question": "You are sent to court for an adjournment, and the judge asks you a question about the case that you cannot answer. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Stays calm and respectful, and never guesses or misleads the court", "Says you will take instructions and asks for time", "Notes exactly what was asked", "Reports to the senior lawyer at once"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "78eea13f-9d82-51af-8025-6d4e49ce6ccc", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Company law", "question": "A company client asks how to make sure it follows every law that applies to it. How would you build a simple compliance checklist?", "key_points": ["Lists the laws by area: company, employment, tax, environment, sector licences", "Notes each filing, licence or duty with its due date", "Names an owner for each item and tracks it", "Reviews the list when the law or the business changes"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "1a2b0bcf-2a44-5bae-85fe-95570bd0e071", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Ethics", "question": "You find a mistake in a document your firm has already sent to the other side. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Tells the senior lawyer at once and does not hide it", "Works out the effect on the client", "Fixes it the right way, such as with a correction letter", "Adds a check to the process so it does not happen again"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "bac6fcd0-8d55-52fb-b47a-7367be304d47", "role": "legal-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Contracts", "question": "A client wants to end a contract early because the other side keeps delivering late. How do you advise?", "key_points": ["Reads the termination and notice clauses first", "Checks the evidence for each late delivery", "Considers breach and remedies under the Contract Act 1872", "Advises on risk, cost and a negotiated way out before going to court"], "source_url": "https://bdlaws.minlaw.gov.bd/act-26.html", "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "0807997a-32a1-5f6e-bea4-b475bb7857f5", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Colour and print", "question": "What is the difference between RGB and CMYK, and when does it matter?", "key_points": ["RGB is light, for screens; CMYK is ink, for print", "Some bright RGB colours cannot be printed and come out dull", "Design print work in CMYK, or convert early and check a proof", "Ask the printer which colour profile to use"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "4e4a0a30-dc83-5c69-aad2-6733593e5ac3", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Typography", "question": "Why would you choose one typeface over another?", "key_points": ["It fits the purpose and the reader: a poster, a report, a phone screen", "It is easy to read at the size it will be used", "It matches the brand's tone", "It has the weights and characters needed, including Bangla if required"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "17c7b5c7-13f9-50ec-91a7-85b49cfbb94b", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Process", "question": "Walk me through your process from brief to final file.", "key_points": ["Read the brief and ask about the goal, the audience and the limits", "Research and rough sketches before the computer", "Show a few options, get feedback, then refine", "Prepare final files in the right size, format and colour mode"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "411b5ba3-c5bf-57dc-827d-3fd4b4ec7b72", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Clients", "question": "A client says 'make it pop'. What do you ask them?", "key_points": ["Ask what they mean: brighter, bigger, more contrast, or more attention", "Ask who the audience is and what they should notice first", "Show two quick options so the feedback becomes concrete"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "dca9bee0-b36a-5525-aa80-0c37b1094157", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Craft", "question": "How do you design something that works on a billboard and on a phone?", "key_points": ["One simple idea with one main message", "Large, bold type and strong contrast", "Few elements, so it reads from far away and on a small screen", "Check it at real size and as a small thumbnail"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "6badbf8c-5c0e-5649-90b1-ba8917e3a7f4", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Craft", "question": "What makes a logo still work at sixteen pixels?", "key_points": ["A simple shape without thin lines or small details", "Strong contrast and a clear outline", "A simpler version of the logo for very small sizes", "Test it as a browser tab icon or app icon"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "9109bb96-a62b-527a-a49c-84887933a5b0", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Typography", "question": "How would you handle Bangla and English in the same layout?", "key_points": ["Pick Bangla and English fonts that look balanced in weight and size", "Bangla usually needs more line height for marks above and below the letters", "Keep a clear hierarchy so the reader knows what to read first", "Check that joined letters render correctly in the final file"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "f9d6cc03-6f7e-55dd-990e-5eb519550f39", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Clients", "question": "A client has rejected three rounds. How do you get the project back on track?", "key_points": ["Go back to the brief and agree what success looks like", "Ask for specific feedback on what is not working", "Show a few clearly different directions, not small changes", "Agree the remaining rounds and dates in writing"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "7271ddea-7d3e-54cf-aac4-d96cb6515a6d", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Process", "question": "How do you decide when a design is finished?", "key_points": ["It meets the brief and the goal", "Nothing can be removed without losing meaning", "It has been checked at real size, with real content, by fresh eyes", "The client has agreed it and the files are ready"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "35095ebd-3cb8-5e87-bf7b-6030e173dcf9", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Colour and print", "question": "What is bleed, and why does a print file need it?", "key_points": ["Extra image or colour that runs past the trim line", "It stops thin white edges when the printer cuts the sheet", "Keep text and logos inside the safe area"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "af176218-b94d-5096-ac3c-eba0ba7adaa9", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Process", "question": "How do you choose what goes in your portfolio for a job like this?", "key_points": ["A few strong pieces that fit the employer's kind of work", "Shows the process, not only the final image", "At least one real brief or client job", "You can explain each piece in a minute"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "a6ee7e70-282a-557d-923c-b2bbdf811369", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Craft", "question": "A brand needs one campaign as a Facebook post, a story and a print poster. How do you adapt the design?", "key_points": ["Start with one strong idea and a clear hierarchy", "Rework the layout for each size; do not just stretch it", "Keep text short so it reads on a small phone screen", "Export the right size, format and colour mode for each one"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "e427e9cc-7570-5979-8add-870953bea5ec", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Colour and print", "question": "What do you check before you send a file to an offset printer?", "key_points": ["CMYK mode and the colour profile the printer asks for", "Images at print resolution; fonts embedded or outlined", "Bleed, trim marks and the safe area", "A printed proof signed off before the full run"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "7313cae9-00ac-55e8-a007-a4073c37516c", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Branding", "question": "A small business wants a full brand identity in two weeks on a very small budget. What do you deliver?", "key_points": ["Agree priorities first: logo, colours, type and a few key templates", "Write down the scope, rounds and dates before starting", "A short guide so other people use the brand correctly", "Leave the extras for a second phase"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "56665faf-4601-51ac-9eb7-5a60509ffc46", "role": "graphic-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Clients", "question": "A client sends you another brand's design and asks you to make the same. How do you respond?", "key_points": ["Explain the risk: copying can break copyright and makes the brand look like someone else", "Find out what they like about it: the colour, the mood or the layout", "Offer an original design that keeps that feeling", "Keep the conversation polite and in writing"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "7d878834-d8a6-5937-b878-3d25bc62ba75", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Process", "question": "What is the difference between UI and UX?", "key_points": ["UX: how the whole experience works and feels for the user", "UI: the screens, layout, type, colour and controls", "Both start from what the user is trying to do"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "79821f9e-3ae4-5760-82ef-603206a39200", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Wireframes", "question": "What is a wireframe, and why make one before a detailed design?", "key_points": ["A simple layout of a screen without the final visuals", "Fast to change, so ideas are tested cheaply", "Keeps the focus on structure and flow first"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "5fa26222-7f2a-599a-b605-1c8e6910bf8c", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Research", "question": "How would you find out what users need before you design?", "key_points": ["Talks to real users, or watches them use the current app", "Looks at data: support complaints, app reviews, analytics", "Writes down the main problems and goals", "Checks ideas with more than one or two people"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "76cd7d4c-4510-56d2-bf53-5985a4b45a9b", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Accessibility", "question": "What makes text and buttons easy to use on a small phone?", "key_points": ["Readable text size and strong colour contrast", "Large tap targets with space between them", "Clear labels, not icons alone", "Testing on a real low-cost phone"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "ca67daef-9464-5f12-a69e-3d02259637fa", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Design systems", "question": "What is a design system, and why does a team use one?", "key_points": ["Shared components, styles and rules for the whole product", "Keeps screens consistent and faster to build", "Designers and developers use the same names"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "8eda6df2-e3c0-5e12-8774-858323d19330", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Usability testing", "question": "How would you run a usability test with five users and almost no budget?", "key_points": ["Picks a few key tasks for users to try", "Watches quietly and asks them to think aloud, without helping", "Notes where they hesitate or fail", "Fixes the biggest problems first and tests again"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "4e857b35-2cbc-58ac-b079-b188d4491379", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Localisation", "question": "Bangla labels are often longer than the English ones. How do you design for both?", "key_points": ["Leaves room for longer text and avoids fixed-width buttons", "Tests every screen with real Bangla text, not placeholder text", "Chooses a font that shows Bangla clearly at small sizes", "Lets text wrap without breaking the layout"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "2ce09fc9-c849-56a3-a760-4e78decf8a37", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Research", "question": "You are designing a wallet app for people using a smartphone for the first time. What would you do differently?", "key_points": ["One main action per screen and very simple steps", "Icons with words, and Bangla first where users prefer it", "A clear check before money moves, and easy help or undo", "Tests with real users from that group, including people who read little"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "6e77721a-69ff-5473-aeb0-943fc9ba3bd6", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Handoff", "question": "How do you hand off a design so developers can build it correctly?", "key_points": ["Specs for spacing, sizes, colours and fonts from the design system", "Every state: empty, loading, error and long text", "Notes on behaviour and edge cases", "Stays available for questions and reviews the build"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "6bd3f640-02bc-5da8-8d84-44f0e79aec91", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Process", "question": "How do you design a screen that still works on a cheap Android phone over slow mobile data?", "key_points": ["Few, light images, with text shown first", "Clear loading and offline states", "No heavy animations", "Tests on a real low-end phone and a slow network"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "c070ced9-c730-5b7c-903b-11a33c2baedf", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Usability testing", "question": "Your test shows users fail at a step the product manager loves. How do you handle it?", "key_points": ["Shows the evidence: clips, quotes, how many users failed", "Keeps the focus on the user's goal, not on who is right", "Offers one or two alternatives to test quickly", "Agrees how success will be measured"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "1478476f-d97c-599d-a8e2-e28fd78cd0e2", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Process", "question": "You have one week to design a feature that normally takes a month. What do you cut, and what do you keep?", "key_points": ["Keeps the core user task and the riskiest question", "Cuts polish and side features for a later version", "Reuses parts from the design system", "Tests the core flow quickly with a few users"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "cff38dba-44d9-5da1-b42b-44f25d80cb83", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Accessibility", "question": "How would you make an app work for someone who uses a screen reader?", "key_points": ["Every control has a clear label", "A logical reading order and headings", "Colour is never the only way to show meaning", "Tests with the phone's screen reader turned on"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "3e0ce18e-f1f0-5637-8a42-9837160e202e", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Design systems", "question": "Two designers built the same button in different ways and the app now looks inconsistent. How do you fix it and stop it happening again?", "key_points": ["Audits the screens to list every version", "Agrees one component with clear rules and states", "Puts it in the shared library and replaces the old versions", "Adds a review step before new components are added"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "ec3aaa49-9bb1-5fab-ad27-ba1456209659", "role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Research", "question": "After launch, many users stop at the sign-up screen. How do you find out why, and what do you change?", "key_points": ["Looks at the data: exactly where people stop", "Watches or calls a few users who dropped off", "Checks common causes: too many fields, an OTP that never arrives, unclear errors", "Changes one thing at a time and measures the result"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "ff4f79d2-2904-5bf9-a659-b89437f2c9ec", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Audience", "question": "How do you decide who you are writing for?", "key_points": ["Asks the brief or the client who will read it, and why", "Thinks about the reader's language level, needs and where they read", "Writes one sentence describing that reader before starting"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "f56effb6-3819-5828-86f4-692fa0c32ff0", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Craft", "question": "What makes a headline work?", "key_points": ["Clear and specific: the reader knows what they will get", "Short, with strong words and no clickbait", "Fits the place it appears: search, social media or print", "Tested in a few versions when possible"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "f2f57970-ed8f-52b6-adef-d4733f97a865", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Research", "question": "How do you research a topic you know nothing about?", "key_points": ["Starts with trusted sources: official sites, experts, good reports", "Reads widely first, then notes the key facts and open questions", "Checks each fact against more than one source", "Asks an expert to check when the topic is technical"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "aad3d648-8264-5bd1-ac04-9c8fdea82091", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "SEO and reach", "question": "How do you write for search without writing badly?", "key_points": ["Writes for the reader first, then fits search terms in naturally", "Finds what people really search for, in English and in Bangla", "Clear headings, a useful answer early, and good links", "Never stuffs keywords"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "b09db7cb-77d7-5cc3-b916-b2dd22d78976", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "SEO and reach", "question": "An article got no readers. How do you find out why?", "key_points": ["Checks the data: views, traffic sources, time on page, where people left", "Asks whether the topic is something people want or search for", "Checks the headline, the timing and where it was shared", "Changes one thing and tries again"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "02bd8d63-6dfc-50ad-a37a-a9b554338f94", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Voice", "question": "How do you keep one brand voice across several writers?", "key_points": ["A short style guide: tone, words to use and avoid, examples", "Templates and good examples to copy", "One editor who checks every piece for voice", "Regular feedback with the writers"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "029ce716-679d-5dc8-92f8-2ed9a2eedb7e", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Craft", "question": "Turn a technical document into something a customer can read. How do you start?", "key_points": ["Finds out who the customer is and what they need to do", "Pulls out the few key points and drops the jargon", "Uses short steps, examples and plain words", "Asks a real customer or a colleague to test it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "a941ba61-4389-5be2-a838-02832cb82636", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Editing", "question": "How do you decide what to cut?", "key_points": ["Cuts anything that does not serve the reader's goal", "Removes repeats, filler words and long warm-ups", "Keeps the facts and examples that prove the point", "Reads it aloud; whatever you skip, cut"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "d60297db-a4fe-504f-9ad8-4a2cf98e70f4", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Voice", "question": "How do you write for a Bangladeshi audience in English without sounding foreign?", "key_points": ["Plain, simple English without foreign slang or idioms", "Local examples: places, prices in taka, festivals, daily life", "Uses Bangla words the way readers do, where it fits the brand", "Tests the draft with local readers"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "ba3d6bb4-311b-5faf-bd95-7432e1de7d1c", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Editing", "question": "How do you check your own work before you send it?", "key_points": ["Reads it aloud, or again after a break", "Checks facts, names and numbers against the source", "Uses a checklist: spelling, grammar, links, style guide", "Asks someone else to read it when it matters"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "3fab1dbd-67bd-59b7-a836-0138234d1a39", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Audience", "question": "How is writing for a website different from a Facebook post or a printed brochure?", "key_points": ["Website: easy to scan, clear headings, search terms", "Facebook: short, with a hook in the first line, made for a phone", "Print: fixed space, careful layout, no links", "Same message, different length and tone"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "04bd0233-0895-5c65-afff-cde57b7cf3ac", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Craft", "question": "In a writing test you get forty minutes to write a 300-word product description. How do you use the time?", "key_points": ["A few minutes on the brief: reader, goal, main message", "A quick outline before writing", "Writes, then leaves time to edit and proofread", "Stays inside the word count"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "c1b3fd60-1903-5f34-8434-6a7ced253cbd", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Translation", "question": "You must turn an English campaign into Bangla. Do you translate word for word? Why or why not?", "key_points": ["Translates the meaning and the feeling, not each word", "Uses the Bangla readers really use, formal or everyday, to fit the brand", "Checks that names, numbers and calls to action still work", "Asks a native reader to check before it goes out"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "a10f31b4-ffb2-51b5-b214-49c48d5d9988", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Editing", "question": "An editor rewrites most of your article, and you disagree with some changes. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Reads the changes calmly and looks for the reasons", "Accepts the ones that improve it and learns from the pattern", "Raises one or two changes that alter the meaning, with reasons", "Agrees how you will work together next time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "d5794ba0-4e09-5b98-a578-64fbdfc670a4", "role": "content-writer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Ethics", "question": "A client asks you to write reviews of their product as if they came from real customers. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Declines politely: fake reviews mislead readers", "Explains the risk to the brand's trust if it comes out", "Offers honest options: ask real customers, write case studies", "Keeps the conversation in writing"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "74203c49-bea4-51e1-8115-acedcc2b3862", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Lesson planning", "question": "How do you plan a forty-minute lesson?", "key_points": ["Starts with one clear learning goal students can reach", "A short opening, teaching, practice, then a check at the end", "Plans the timing and materials, and what to drop if time runs short"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "9f9d9d31-806e-57c9-b220-220161e8b7b5", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Classroom management", "question": "How do you set rules on the first day with a new class?", "key_points": ["A few clear rules, explained and agreed with the class", "Shows what good behaviour looks like", "Applies the rules the same way for everyone", "Learns names quickly"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "85dc2342-45ed-5266-95a0-72b4d5bd612b", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Assessment", "question": "What is the difference between formative and summative assessment? Give an example of each.", "key_points": ["Formative: checks during learning, to guide the next step", "Summative: measures what was learned at the end, such as a term exam", "Formative examples: questions in class, short quizzes, exit slips"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "01786b9e-0a38-51d1-8d91-c0b64a6d8fd3", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Teaching career", "question": "How are teachers hired for non-government schools in Bangladesh, and where do you check the current rules?", "key_points": ["Entry-level posts at non-government schools go through NTRCA", "NTRCA runs the registration and selection process", "The rules have changed in recent years, so read NTRCA's current notices", "Shows you know the steps but care most about teaching"], "source_url": "https://ntrca.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "48894f0f-d75d-53d1-823e-a16fbde48f53", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Parents", "question": "How do you talk to parents about their child's progress?", "key_points": ["Starts with something the child does well", "Gives one or two specific areas to work on, with examples", "Agrees simple steps for home and for school", "Keeps it private and respectful"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "be201236-e07d-5f7c-9c3e-21e1d3bd646c", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Classroom management", "question": "You have a class of sixty students. How do you keep everyone involved?", "key_points": ["Pair and group work, so more students get to speak", "Asks questions across the whole room, not only the front rows", "Quick checks such as hands up or short written answers", "Clear routines that save time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "873ad547-3ca6-5151-a586-957836adec50", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Different learners", "question": "Some students in your class are far ahead and some are far behind. How do you teach both?", "key_points": ["Finds levels early with a short check", "Gives tasks at different levels with the same goal", "Pairs stronger and weaker students with care", "Gives extra support time to those behind"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "bdae640e-af85-5419-bac8-0a7a2d37b19a", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Lesson planning", "question": "The national curriculum or a textbook changes. How do you get ready to teach the new version?", "key_points": ["Reads the new textbook and teacher guide from NCTB, the official source", "Finds what changed: content, activities and assessment", "Joins training and plans with other teachers", "Explains the changes to students and parents"], "source_url": "https://nctb.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "62ede48c-1163-5dd9-9b59-eedf99a38baf", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Different learners", "question": "How would you teach an English lesson to students who rarely speak English outside class?", "key_points": ["Simple English and plenty of speaking practice in pairs", "Brief Bangla to explain a hard point, then back to English", "Topics linked to students' daily life", "Praises effort to build confidence"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "7d920924-7340-513a-976a-ea412acfabd4", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Assessment", "question": "How do you give feedback on written work so that students actually improve?", "key_points": ["Comments on a few key points, not every error", "Says what is good and gives one clear next step", "Gives time in class to act on the feedback", "Checks the next piece of work for progress"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "8558d077-e88a-5e8e-86c9-ac0483abd508", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Ethics", "question": "A parent asks you to give private tuition to their child, who is in your own class. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Government policy bars teachers from privately tutoring students of their own institution", "Explains politely why: fairness in class and in marking", "Offers extra help at school, open to every student who needs it", "Tells the head teacher if the pressure continues"], "source_url": "https://www.thedailystar.net/country/news/teachers-cannot-run-coaching-classes-1698811", "sort_order": 11},
