{"id": "cf191c37-a28c-5373-83be-19be37079384", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Parents", "question": "A parent is angry about their child's low marks and says you marked unfairly. How do you handle it?", "key_points": ["Listens calmly and thanks them for coming", "Shows the paper, the marking scheme and where marks were lost", "Agrees a plan to help the child improve", "Corrects any real mistake openly"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "f9893517-50aa-5305-82db-864b490dd86c", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Different learners", "question": "You think a student may have a learning difficulty, such as trouble with reading. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Observes and notes specific examples over some weeks", "Adjusts teaching: more time, clear print, spoken answers", "Talks to the head teacher and parents gently, without labels", "Suggests a specialist check where one is available"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "0760818d-e85e-584a-b6f4-82f9afd8977f", "role": "school-teacher", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Assessment", "question": "Your students score well by memorising but cannot explain the ideas. How would you change your teaching?", "key_points": ["Asks why and how questions, not only what", "Uses activities: explain to a partner, solve a new problem, real-life examples", "Changes some test questions to check understanding", "Explains the reason to students and parents who expect memorising"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "0653b08c-4cc5-5e80-ba7c-b335badb4f8f", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "About you", "question": "Introduce yourself to the viva board in about one minute.", "key_points": ["Name, home district, university and subject, in a clear order", "One strength or achievement that fits public service", "Calm, polite and natural, not a memorised speech"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "62dcd95a-19bd-5d27-906f-660e09642b18", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Your subject", "question": "How can your university subject help you as a government officer?", "key_points": ["Two or three real links between your subject and public work", "One example, such as using data for planning", "Shows you will keep learning outside your subject"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "6df3336b-88f3-53f6-98b9-8c92825e1c82", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Cadre choice", "question": "Why did you choose the cadre at the top of your BCS choice list?", "key_points": ["Honest reasons linked to your skills and interests", "Shows you know what officers in that cadre actually do", "Shows you would also serve well in the other cadres you chose"], "source_url": "https://bpsc.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "7c5f15ae-8931-56d9-b54b-c23945d0560f", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "BCS process", "question": "What are the stages of the BCS examination, and what does each one test?", "key_points": ["Preliminary: a multiple-choice screening test", "Written: longer papers, plus subject papers for technical and professional cadres", "Viva: a board interview on you, your subject and your judgement", "Rules can change between cycles, so read the current circular from BPSC"], "source_url": "https://bpsc.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 4},
