{"id": "c3c99883-0844-5a5c-8ca6-22f60dd8a670", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Governance basics", "question": "What does good citizen service mean to you, and how would you make a government office easier to use?", "key_points": ["Clear information on what each service needs and how long it takes", "Fewer visits: online forms and payments where possible", "Polite, equal treatment for every citizen", "A simple way to complain and get an answer"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "fa49df9a-7677-5363-bb96-710dc0b537a9", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Development", "question": "Pick one public service in rural areas, such as health or schooling. What is its biggest challenge, and what would you try?", "key_points": ["Names one service and a specific problem", "Uses evidence: what you have seen, or official data", "Suggests a practical, low-cost step", "Says how you would know it worked"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "1b58611d-7712-5eac-be30-97aaabd9eafc", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Situational judgement", "question": "You are posted to a remote upazila far from home. How would you settle in and start work?", "key_points": ["Accepts postings as part of the job, with a positive attitude", "Learns the area: people, offices and the main problems", "Builds working relationships with local staff and community members", "Keeps a healthy routine to stay effective"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
