{"id": "c88bc7cd-335a-5890-befa-7725d01694cc", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Cadre choice", "question": "If you do not get your first-choice cadre, how will you feel and what will you do?", "key_points": ["Honest but positive: every cadre is a chance to serve", "Shows interest in what the given cadre does", "Plans to do the work well and keep learning"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "5daa85d2-056a-52ca-958b-af1c867823d9", "role": "civil-service-officer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Governance basics", "question": "A citizen complains that someone in your office asked for money to process a file. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Takes the complaint seriously and records it", "Protects the person who complained", "Checks the facts fairly and quickly", "Acts under the service rules and reports to the right authority"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "98096681-5a2c-5c2c-8df5-d62fcaa134ff", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Statistics", "question": "What is the difference between the mean and the median, and when does it matter?", "key_points": ["Mean: the total divided by the count; median: the middle value", "Outliers pull the mean but barely move the median", "Use the median for skewed data such as salaries or house prices"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "0449557d-76a5-521a-b1f0-b77c59c6dbf3", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Data quality", "question": "You are handed a spreadsheet of sales. What are the first three things you check?", "key_points": ["What each column means, and whether the totals look sensible", "Missing values, duplicates and wrong data types", "The date range, and whether every branch or region is there", "What question the data must answer"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "b154546f-3e96-5c85-842e-d2aa595a7878", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "SQL", "question": "Explain what a JOIN does to somebody who has never written SQL.", "key_points": ["A JOIN puts rows from two tables together using a shared column", "Example: orders matched to customers by customer ID", "An inner join keeps only matches; a left join keeps every row of the first table"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "bf0b6132-1854-5182-b3d2-83a8344a6104", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Data quality", "question": "A number in your report looks wrong. Walk me through how you check it.", "key_points": ["Recalculates it from the raw data, step by step", "Checks filters, joins and date ranges for mistakes", "Compares it with another source or last month's figure", "Says so openly if it was wrong, and corrects it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "c9567a13-c74d-57f7-8712-0c006a0ba4aa", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Experiments", "question": "How would you find out which of two versions of a page performs better?", "key_points": ["An A/B test: users split at random between the two versions", "One main metric agreed before the test starts", "Runs long enough for enough users, and checks the result is not chance", "Watches for other changes running at the same time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "bc01d528-ef94-51c0-8691-2abede031a69", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Dashboards", "question": "Your dashboard shows a spike last Tuesday. How do you work out whether it is real?", "key_points": ["Checks for data problems first: duplicates, a broken feed, a changed definition", "Looks at the raw rows behind the spike", "Looks for a real cause: a campaign, a holiday, a sale", "Confirms with the team that owns the data"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "6a899293-19a1-5abf-997e-60f951cd050f", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Framing", "question": "A manager asks 'why did revenue drop?'. How do you turn that into an analysis?", "key_points": ["Asks how much, since when, and compared with what", "Splits revenue into parts: customers, orders, price, product, region", "Rules out data problems before business causes", "Ends with a short answer and a next step"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "43d9f973-0674-5cd0-8333-ac6148bb57af", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Statistics", "question": "What is the difference between correlation and causation? Give an example from your own work.", "key_points": ["Correlation: two things move together; causation: one makes the other happen", "A third factor can drive both, such as Eid raising both ad spend and sales", "Gives a real example from a project", "Only a controlled test can show cause"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "a1d66077-c766-5f78-b1b9-21c40407f626", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Data quality", "question": "A third of a column is missing. What are your options, and how do you choose?", "key_points": ["Finds out why it is missing, and whether that is random", "Options: drop the rows, fill with a sensible value, or flag as missing", "The choice depends on how the column is used and how much it matters", "Records the choice and shows its effect on the results"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "11baf5e4-99cf-51c1-82d7-c4149956abcb", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Excel", "question": "Which Excel functions do you use most for cleaning and summarising data?", "key_points": ["Lookups: XLOOKUP or VLOOKUP, or INDEX with MATCH", "Summaries: pivot tables, SUMIFS and COUNTIFS", "Cleaning: TRIM, text functions, removing duplicates", "Shows one real task done with them"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "128a4393-28ff-5b89-b48f-ce7a44f49d44", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "SQL", "question": "What is the difference between WHERE and HAVING in SQL?", "key_points": ["WHERE filters rows before grouping", "HAVING filters groups after GROUP BY", "Example: months with total sales above a set amount need HAVING"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "72eaaaf6-514c-530a-9643-14f35dba0ad6", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Data quality", "question": "Customer names in your data are written in Bangla and English, with many spellings. How do you count unique customers?", "key_points": ["Does not rely on the name; uses a stable ID such as phone or customer number", "Standardises text: trims spaces, one case, common spelling fixes", "Uses fuzzy matching with care, and checks a sample by hand", "Reports how many records could not be matched"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "7d8bdd26-9310-5ce0-a5b3-6b71f86457d3", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Modelling", "question": "How would you build a simple model to forecast next month's sales?", "key_points": ["Starts from the history: trend and seasonal peaks such as Eid", "Tries a simple baseline first, such as the same month last year or a moving average", "Checks the error on past months before trusting it", "Gives a range, not just one number"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "55300761-a1bc-5eef-84db-424b4e92504c", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Modelling", "question": "Your model is very accurate on training data but poor on new data. What is happening, and what do you do?", "key_points": ["Overfitting: the model learned noise in the training data", "Uses a separate test set or cross-validation", "Simplifies the model, adds data or uses regularisation", "Checks for leakage: inputs that would not be known at prediction time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "87e1037b-eaa2-5597-8b2a-5c1ebeadf7ef", "role": "data-analyst", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Dashboards", "question": "Senior managers want one daily MIS dashboard for sales, but each team defines sales differently. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Lists each definition and where it comes from", "Agrees one definition with the owners and writes it down", "Shows the definition on the dashboard itself", "Reconciles the new number with old reports before launch"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "1b3d09d2-bc21-5659-8caf-bc3d6b8ca2f8", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Orders", "question": "What does a merchandiser do in a garment factory, from order to shipment?", "key_points": ["Turns the buyer's order into a plan the factory can follow", "Books fabric and trims, chases samples, keeps the time and action plan", "Talks every day with the buyer, production, quality and commercial teams", "Owns the order until it ships and payment is clear"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "e4ed396a-a011-5a3d-b709-5dc17e322c14", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Costing", "question": "What is the difference between an FOB order and a CM order?", "key_points": ["FOB: the factory buys fabric and trims and quotes one price per piece", "CM: the buyer supplies the materials and the factory charges for cutting and making", "FOB means more work and more risk for the merchandiser: sourcing, booking, payment"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "a64c8e3d-da51-5f2f-94e7-48c3f9b58ea9", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Materials", "question": "What does GSM mean on a fabric, and why does the buyer care?", "key_points": ["Grams per square metre: how heavy the fabric is", "Higher GSM usually means thicker fabric and a higher cost", "The order fixes the GSM, so fabric outside it can be rejected"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "abb50773-7abe-59eb-bfc3-c7e76b9ab762", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Orders", "question": "What samples does an order usually go through before bulk production?", "key_points": ["Proto, fit, size set, pre-production, then shipment sample; names vary by buyer", "Each one answers a question: style, fit, sizes, final approval", "Bulk cutting should not start before pre-production approval"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "3d851125-9b83-5543-8cd3-8d39b68d8def", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Orders", "question": "What is a tech pack, and what do you check first when you receive one?", "key_points": ["The buyer's full description: sketches, measurements, fabric, trims, labels, packing", "First check what is missing or unclear", "Send questions early, in writing, before costing or sampling"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "3bc28752-5d85-568e-9414-dd81601266da", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Costing", "question": "How would you build the FOB price of a basic T-shirt?", "key_points": ["Fabric: consumption per dozen times fabric price, plus wastage", "Add trims, any print or wash, the cost of making and overheads", "Add commercial costs such as testing, transport and bank charges, then profit", "Check the total against the buyer's target price"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "e32c428a-d040-5366-bcb7-49423eb7b195", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Time and action", "question": "What is a time and action calendar, and what do you do when one step slips?", "key_points": ["It lists every step from order to shipment, with a date and an owner", "When a step slips, work out the effect on the ship date at once", "Look for ways to recover: steps in parallel, more lines, faster approvals", "Tell the buyer early, with a new plan"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "b611a44a-a2c3-5eb2-a850-a272fd37205c", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Shipment and payment", "question": "What is a letter of credit, and why does a garment exporter use a back-to-back LC?", "key_points": ["An LC is a bank's promise to pay when the documents match the terms", "A back-to-back LC uses the export LC to open import LCs for fabric and trims", "It lets the factory buy materials without paying cash up front", "Small document mistakes can delay payment"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "a58bb827-f540-50be-b62e-d352cca6fc99", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Materials", "question": "An order has five colours and six sizes. How do you work out how much fabric to book?", "key_points": ["Use the colour and size breakdown of the order quantity", "Take consumption per size from the pattern or marker", "Add wastage and allow for shrinkage after washing", "Book by colour, and check the mill's minimum order"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "8bd4164f-3283-549a-81ea-44de3939cd41", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Shipment and payment", "question": "What is a UD, and why do you need one before importing fabric for an export order?", "key_points": ["A utilisation declaration issued by the factory's trade body for each export order", "It lets a bonded factory bring in fabric and trims without paying import duty", "It needs the export LC or contract, the back-to-back LCs and the material details", "Check the trade body's current checklist; much of the process is now online"], "source_url": "https://www.bgmea.com.bd/", "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "ab60a920-e308-5098-92fb-bb3d15747eee", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Shipment and payment", "question": "Production is five days late and the vessel cut-off at Chattogram is fixed. What are your options, and how do you choose?", "key_points": ["Find the real cause first: materials, capacity, quality or approvals", "Options: overtime, more lines, an approved subcontractor, a split shipment, air freight", "Compare each by cost, quality risk and who pays", "Agree the plan with the buyer in writing before acting"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "a4128536-07dd-5184-bb82-33f5e967a155", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Quality", "question": "The final inspection fails on AQL. What happens next, and what do you do?", "key_points": ["AQL is a sampling rule: too many defects in the sample means the whole lot fails", "Find the defect types, then check every piece and repair or replace", "Book a re-inspection and update the shipment plan", "Fix the root cause so the next order does not repeat it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "8538c75b-595e-5910-9fdd-0fcff65039ca", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Costing", "question": "The buyer's target price is below your cost. How do you respond?", "key_points": ["Break down the cost to see where the gap is", "Offer changes that keep quality: fabric or trim choices, simpler construction", "Know the factory's lowest acceptable price and do not go under it", "Explain your reasons and give options, to keep the relationship"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "7ec86584-948a-5aab-8017-109317f93afb", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Buyer communication", "question": "After the pre-production sample is approved, the buyer asks to change the buttons. How do you handle it?", "key_points": ["Check what it affects: cost, lead time, trims already booked", "Confirm the change and its cost and time impact in writing", "Update the tech pack, trims order and plan, and tell production and quality", "Never change bulk on a verbal request"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "fc60044c-e7f7-545e-bdf0-e60b492070b7", "role": "apparel-merchandiser", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Compliance", "question": "Why do buyers audit factories for social and safety compliance, and how does it affect your work?", "key_points": ["Buyers need proof that workers are treated fairly and buildings are safe", "Checks became much stricter after the Rana Plaza collapse in 2013", "An unapproved subcontractor or a failed audit can stop orders", "Place work only in approved units and keep records clean"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "d9799e77-63ee-5f8e-9765-0c67554f51d7", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Fibre and yarn", "question": "What is the difference between knit and woven fabric? Name a garment made from each.", "key_points": ["Knit is loops from one yarn and stretches; woven crosses two sets of yarn", "Knit: T-shirt, polo. Woven: shirt, trousers, denim", "Factories usually specialise in one or the other"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "1713b755-d4bd-5bd3-81f7-36288575582e", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Fibre and yarn", "question": "What does yarn count mean, and which is finer: 30s or 40s cotton yarn?", "key_points": ["Count tells you how fine or coarse the yarn is", "In the cotton count system, a higher number means a finer yarn", "40s is finer than 30s and gives a lighter, smoother fabric"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "6862c61a-f38b-5d17-bfbe-06c3cce0f8db", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Knitting", "question": "What is the difference between single jersey, rib and interlock fabric?", "key_points": ["Single jersey: one needle bed, light, curls at the edge, used for T-shirts", "Rib: two needle beds, stretches across, used for collars, cuffs and fitted tops", "Interlock: two layers knitted together, thicker and smooth on both sides"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "37888ad3-04e0-5229-8e73-2d8013f2c04b", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Dyeing and finishing", "question": "Why is cotton usually dyed with reactive dyes, and what are the main steps?", "key_points": ["Reactive dyes bond with the cotton fibre, so the colour holds well in washing", "Pretreatment first: scouring and bleaching", "Dyeing with salt and alkali, then washing off and soaping", "Washing off removes loose dye that would bleed later"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "c81bb67b-e66a-5cb1-ad93-72ea2ebd5416", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Fabric defects", "question": "Name three common knit fabric defects and one cause of each.", "key_points": ["Holes: a broken needle or weak yarn", "Barre or stripes: mixed yarn lots or uneven tension", "Needle lines or drop stitches: faulty needles or sinkers", "Oil spots: poor machine cleaning or oiling"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "d1c45942-5a95-50b1-bded-42f90970a4eb", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Process control", "question": "The shade of a dyed batch does not match the approved lab dip. What do you check?", "key_points": ["Recipe and weighing: the right dyes, amounts and liquor ratio", "Process: temperature, time, pH, salt and alkali dosing", "Fabric: the same yarn lot and the same pretreatment", "Decide with the lab whether to add dye to correct it or strip and re-dye"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "bc21d0d8-5477-5b30-a959-88d234e541ff", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Dyeing and finishing", "question": "What is a lab dip, and why must the buyer approve it before bulk dyeing?", "key_points": ["A small sample dyed to match the buyer's colour standard", "Checked in a light box under the buyer's chosen light sources", "Approval fixes the recipe so the bulk can match it", "Saves the cost of re-dyeing a whole batch"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "164ef240-747f-5c00-9e2b-3b0bb604261b", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Knitting", "question": "What do you check during a shift to keep a knitting machine making good fabric?", "key_points": ["Yarn: the right count and lot, with no mixing", "Stitch length and GSM against the order", "Needles, sinkers and tension, with regular cleaning and oiling", "Record faults and machine stops in the shift report"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "1e8e5d67-d8fc-584a-a755-b8d076813b57", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "ETP", "question": "Why does a dyeing factory need an effluent treatment plant, and what do you do if it stops working?", "key_points": ["Dyeing waste water carries colour and chemicals that harm rivers and farmland", "The Department of Environment ties a dyeing unit's environmental clearance to a working ETP", "If it stops, report at once and never release untreated water", "Check the current environment rules for discharge limits; they change"], "source_url": "https://doe.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "ba565522-b289-5564-b86e-f8114878a7ed", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Productivity", "question": "Water, steam and gas costs are rising in the dyeing unit. Where would you look for savings?", "key_points": ["Lower the liquor ratio where the machine and fabric allow", "Aim for right-first-time dyeing: fewer re-dyes save water, energy and time", "Reuse cooling water and fix steam leaks", "Measure use per kilogram of fabric to track progress"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "46eb7334-9642-54aa-a5cb-11a4d9352397", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Fabric defects", "question": "A bulk batch comes out with patchy, uneven shade. What could cause it, and what do you do?", "key_points": ["Poor pretreatment: fabric not evenly scoured or bleached", "Dye or chemicals added too fast, or the temperature raised too quickly", "Poor liquor flow or an overloaded machine", "Decide if the batch can be levelled or must be stripped, and fix the cause"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "4ad7aa45-635b-5cdd-af43-b86cf8d04291", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Process control", "question": "Gas pressure drops during a dyeing batch and the temperature falls. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Follow the factory's plan and hold the batch safely if you can", "Note the time, temperature and the step reached", "Talk to the lab and the supervisor before restarting or correcting", "Check the shade before unloading and record the cause"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "73ac8611-5b81-5cf3-a82e-1e90b02bcb3f", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Productivity", "question": "Your knitting floor keeps missing its daily output target. How do you find the cause?", "key_points": ["Check machine stops: yarn breaks, needle changes, waiting for yarn", "Check people: absence, skill, shift handover", "Compare by machine and by shift to find patterns", "Fix the biggest loss first and track the result"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "cb052c52-0141-561d-8402-1bb8ffaa2d0b", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Chemicals", "question": "A new worker mixes dye chemicals without gloves or goggles because it is faster. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Stop the work at once, politely", "Explain the risk: burns, eye damage, breathing problems", "Give the right protective equipment and show the safe method", "Report it so the whole team gets the training again"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "46860f99-74a6-5438-9eb1-665815559c30", "role": "textile-production-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Chemicals", "question": "An export buyer asks for safer chemicals and lower water use on their orders. What changes on your floor?", "key_points": ["Choose dyes and chemicals that meet the buyer's restricted substances list", "Keep chemical records the buyer can audit", "Use low liquor ratio machines and right-first-time recipes", "Explain any cost and time impact to the merchandising team"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "fe8c410b-18e5-534e-8d57-c34d588be467", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "AQL inspection", "question": "What is AQL, and how is it used in a final inspection?", "key_points": ["Acceptable quality level: the worst average defect level the buyer accepts", "Lot size and inspection level give the sample size; the AQL table gives the accept and reject numbers", "Defects are counted as critical, major or minor against the buyer's AQL", "Pass or fail is decided on the sample, not on every piece"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "84f0819c-6427-5da9-82db-d6567761e769", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Fabric tests", "question": "What is the 4-point system for fabric inspection?", "key_points": ["Each defect gets 1 to 4 points depending on its length; holes score high", "Points are added per roll and turned into points per 100 square yards", "Each roll's score is compared with the buyer's limit"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "c92f3dfa-bc3a-521b-a214-77680a67a344", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Fabric tests", "question": "What do GSM, shrinkage and colour fastness tests tell you about a fabric?", "key_points": ["GSM: weight per square metre, checked against the order", "Shrinkage: how much the fabric changes size after washing", "Colour fastness: whether colour runs or fades in washing, rubbing or light"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "eb29132c-21bb-517c-bfe3-5d127d0649a1", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Defect types", "question": "What is the difference between a critical, a major and a minor defect?", "key_points": ["Critical: unsafe, such as a broken needle left in the garment", "Major: likely to cause a return, such as an open seam or a stain", "Minor: a small fault that does not stop use or sale", "The buyer's quality manual defines each one"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "cfc19bc0-ab63-5b7e-a9e1-0e671a137dd1", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Measurements", "question": "How do you check garment measurements against the spec sheet?", "key_points": ["Lay the garment flat and measure each point as the spec describes", "Compare with the size chart and the allowed tolerance", "Record every point that is out of tolerance, by size", "Use a checked tape and the same method every time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "9be950a0-9b99-5737-9d32-85423ad7a7e1", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Defect types", "question": "Panels in one garment show a slight shade difference. What causes it, and what do you do?", "key_points": ["Panels cut from different rolls, or from different ends of one roll", "Check shade grouping before cutting and bundle tickets during sewing", "Hold the affected lot and report to production and merchandising", "Fix at the source: group rolls by shade and keep one shade per lay"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "7abe1ada-212e-5c77-84b6-54be1e106fee", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "AQL inspection", "question": "During an inline inspection you find the same defect again and again from one operator. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Show the operator the defect and the right method", "Tell the line supervisor and record it", "Check the next pieces to confirm the fix", "Check whether a machine or attachment is causing it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "1ff13cf3-7493-5443-9ea4-44ea22ac6ba4", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Fabric tests", "question": "A fabric fails the shrinkage test before cutting. What are the options?", "key_points": ["Report the result at once to merchandising and the fabric supplier", "Options: re-finish or compact the fabric, adjust the pattern, or reject it", "Any pattern change needs buyer approval", "Do not cut until the decision is in writing"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "4414e8d7-6948-5643-9fb5-6072a0487254", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Reports", "question": "What goes into a good inspection report?", "key_points": ["Order, style, lot size, sample size and the AQL used", "Defects by type and severity, with photos", "Measurement results and the final pass or fail", "Clear next steps and who signs off"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "4fdd52ae-0f6e-542c-8c96-d7de4d9de335", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Fabric tests", "question": "How do you check that a garment's colour matches the approved standard?", "key_points": ["Use a light box under the buyer's light sources", "Compare with the approved lab dip or swatch, not from memory", "Watch for colours that match in one light and not in another", "Record the result and raise shade problems early"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "e32acb73-8b9f-52bb-a50a-7db0ee434849", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Root cause", "question": "A final inspection fails because of too many stains. How do you find the root cause and stop it happening again?", "key_points": ["Find where the stains are on the garment and in which process they start", "Check machines for oil, how pieces are handled, and clean tables and packing areas", "Ask why again and again until you reach the real cause", "Fix it, then re-inspect and watch the next lots"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "af1a2ec5-001a-5f08-bef9-8f1524ef7312", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Ethics", "question": "A supervisor asks you to pass a lot that is just over the AQL limit because the shipment is tomorrow. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Do not change the result; a false pass risks a claim and the buyer's trust", "Explain the facts and the options: sort, repair, then re-inspect", "Raise it with the quality manager", "Record the decision in writing"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "6766d868-9655-5202-b9a6-13c44c8e32d7", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Measurements", "question": "One size is out of tolerance across the whole lot, a day before the buyer's final inspection. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Find which points are out, and by how much", "Trace the cause: pattern, cutting, sewing or shrinkage in washing", "Decide with production which pieces can be corrected, and sort them", "Tell merchandising early so the buyer is not surprised"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "2fdc1d6d-aff3-5004-abf8-ec449a374882", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Root cause", "question": "Garments come back because the colour bled in the first wash, yet the lab test passed. How do you investigate?", "key_points": ["Check whether the bulk batches were tested, not only the first approval", "Compare the test's washing method with the care label", "Check the washing off after dyeing and any fixing step", "Agree a new test plan for every batch"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "7862d4b7-7fc1-5295-be41-b6be5339f0df", "role": "textile-quality-inspector", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "AQL inspection", "question": "A third-party inspector fails a lot that your team passed. How do you handle it?", "key_points": ["Stay calm and ask to see the defects they found", "Check that both used the same standard, sample size and defect rules", "Accept real findings and arrange sorting and re-inspection", "Find out why your inspection missed them and fix your method"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "4d372a25-39d2-5376-8d59-f97917db1550", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Concrete", "question": "What is curing, and what happens if concrete is not cured properly?", "key_points": ["Curing keeps new concrete wet so the cement keeps hardening", "Common ways: ponding, wet hessian or plastic cover, for the days the spec says", "Poor curing gives cracks, lower strength and a weak surface"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "b62688c9-2339-5dee-bb7a-658047d898f3", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Concrete", "question": "What does a slump test tell you, and how do you do it on site?", "key_points": ["It checks how workable fresh concrete is", "Fill the cone in three layers, rod each layer, lift it and measure the drop", "If the slump is far from the spec, stop and check the water and mix"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "88a18e4b-bff1-5c97-ac5b-483c2297955b", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Reinforcement", "question": "What is clear cover in RCC, and what goes wrong if it is too thin?", "key_points": ["Cover is the concrete between the bars and the outside face", "It protects steel from rust and fire and helps the bond", "Thin cover leads to rust, cracks and spalling"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "6935165a-7ea5-585d-b579-fe31b77c83d3", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Drawings and codes", "question": "What is the difference between an architectural drawing and a structural drawing?", "key_points": ["Architectural: rooms, sizes, doors, windows and finishes", "Structural: foundations, columns, beams, slabs and bar details", "On site you check they agree and raise any clash early"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "6db19cd3-d765-5190-88e5-463a0d8de2ae", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Site practice", "question": "What do you check before you allow a slab to be poured?", "key_points": ["Formwork is level, tight and well propped", "Bars match the drawing and someone has signed it off", "Materials, vibrator, workers and the curing plan are ready"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "e521c528-abb3-5c8e-a36c-3a440432641a", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Quantities", "question": "How do you estimate the bricks for a 10-inch brick wall?", "key_points": ["Find the wall volume and take out doors and windows", "Use brick size plus mortar joint to get bricks per cubic foot or cubic metre", "Add a small wastage allowance and work out the mortar"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "caa2c759-db8f-5fcf-980f-62b3ab52676e", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Concrete", "question": "The cylinder test results come back below the required strength. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Check the test record first: sampling, curing of samples, the lab", "Tell the senior engineer or consultant at once, in writing", "Test the structure itself, then accept, strengthen or remove"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "8d65e593-5795-564f-9adf-74d838d928ae", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Soil and foundations", "question": "Why are piles so common in Dhaka and many parts of Bangladesh?", "key_points": ["Much of the land is soft clay or filled ground with a high water table", "Shallow footings may settle unevenly", "Piles carry the load down to firmer soil"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "66900d82-e527-5e35-bfd0-773924a2d195", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Safety", "question": "What are the biggest safety risks on a building site, and what do you do on your first day?", "key_points": ["Falls from height, falling objects and electric shock", "Check helmets, boots and harnesses are used", "Barricade openings and stop any unsafe work"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "e9cd511b-bd91-5677-9eca-ed554b38ead1", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Site management", "question": "You find workers using less cement than the mix design says. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Get facts first: watch a batch, check stock and records", "Stop that work and talk to the contractor's site in-charge", "Report it in writing and check the work already done"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "12520afc-16c2-54b4-b8d0-f324804b0781", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Drawings and codes", "question": "What is the Bangladesh National Building Code, and how does it affect your work on site?", "key_points": ["It sets minimum rules for design, materials, construction and safety", "Check the current edition on the official site before quoting it", "On site you build to approved drawings designed under it"], "source_url": "https://hbri.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "87438d02-c2cf-5cd6-a980-137cabc39338", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Site management", "question": "The monsoon starts next week and you have an open basement excavation. What is your plan?", "key_points": ["Dewatering pumps with backup power", "Protect the pit sides with shoring or safe slopes and drains", "Watch neighbouring buildings for cracks or settlement"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "e33a9ee3-9896-5906-828c-50e564605719", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Quantities", "question": "How do you prepare a bill of quantities from drawings, and what mistakes are common?", "key_points": ["Break the work into items by trade, each with a clear unit", "Measure in a fixed order so nothing is missed", "Common mistakes: missing items, wrong units, double counting"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "cc0f56a9-37f1-5d18-8299-34129a47bd58", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Site management", "question": "Your site is three weeks behind schedule. How do you find out why and recover?", "key_points": ["Compare planned and actual progress item by item", "Find the critical activities causing the delay", "Tell the client honestly, with a new schedule"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "dec9a08a-d2dd-5628-9a1a-30eb40a1a867", "role": "civil-site-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Concrete", "question": "A week after the formwork is removed, you see a crack in a beam. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Keep the load off and put the props back", "Record the crack: width, length, pattern, photos and date", "Tell the structural engineer and never just plaster over it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "5da7c139-136d-5406-8f3d-b027d799eee8", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Circuits", "question": "What is the difference between AC and DC, and why is AC used for the power grid?", "key_points": ["AC changes direction many times a second; DC flows one way", "Transformers can step AC voltage up and down easily", "High voltage cuts the losses on long lines", "The grid in Bangladesh runs at 50 Hz"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "b67d96f3-068d-5ec5-9329-8a70390f8341", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Transformers", "question": "How does a transformer work, and what is it used for?", "key_points": ["Two coils on an iron core, linked by a changing magnetic field", "The turns ratio sets how much the voltage changes", "Steps voltage up for transmission, such as 132 kV, and down to 33 kV and 11 kV", "Works only on AC"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "e82fb731-fc1e-5a18-9f3b-98566c027e18", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Protection", "question": "What is the difference between a fuse, an MCB and an MCCB?", "key_points": ["Fuse: a wire that melts on a fault and must be replaced", "MCB: a resettable breaker for small currents in homes and panels", "MCCB: higher currents and adjustable settings, for industry", "Choose by current rating, breaking capacity and the load"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "02b32b89-7c08-5a1c-a053-2270f4172829", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Earthing", "question": "What is earthing, and why is it important?", "key_points": ["Connects metal parts and the system to the ground", "Gives fault current a safe path so the protection trips", "Protects people from electric shock", "Check earth resistance regularly, especially in the dry season"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "5f7615ad-5052-552a-b2b1-aaa9cc91b6fe", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Safety", "question": "What does lock-out and tag-out mean?", "key_points": ["Isolate the power source before any work", "Lock the switch and tag it with your name", "Test that the circuit is dead before touching it", "Only the person who fitted the lock removes it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "7b52b34c-1efb-548e-a4e9-16e133c9b299", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Power factor", "question": "What is power factor, and why does a low power factor cost a factory money?", "key_points": ["The ratio of real power in kW to apparent power in kVA", "A low power factor draws more current for the same work", "More current means more losses, bigger cables and possible charges on the bill", "Correct it with capacitor banks sized from a load study"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "08bf8fd6-15d6-5fad-af01-9f819bee63d3", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Generators", "question": "How do you synchronise a generator with the grid or with another generator?", "key_points": ["Match voltage, frequency and phase sequence", "Close the breaker when the phase angle is close to zero", "Use a synchroscope or an automatic synchroniser", "Wrong synchronising causes very high currents and damage"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "da7d55ad-6210-51d9-9b7f-f3ce79fdd8c8", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Substations", "question": "What equipment would you expect in an 11 kV to 0.4 kV substation in a factory?", "key_points": ["HT switchgear, such as a VCB, with protection relays", "A distribution transformer and its protection", "An LT panel with an ACB and outgoing breakers", "Power factor correction, metering and earthing"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "bf885059-f498-5a14-811a-e654a649347a", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Protection", "question": "Explain how an overcurrent relay and an earth fault relay protect a system.", "key_points": ["Overcurrent relay: trips when current stays above a set level for a set time", "Earth fault relay: detects current leaking to earth", "Settings are coordinated so the nearest breaker trips first", "Test the relays and record their settings"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "ee9805d4-cb6b-5b24-b17b-90892b173ca3", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Circuits", "question": "How would you size a cable for a 30 kW motor?", "key_points": ["Work out full-load current from power, voltage and power factor", "Apply derating for temperature, grouping and how it is laid", "Check voltage drop over the cable length", "Check short-circuit capacity, then choose the next standard size"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "40c31aff-1325-5461-acfd-4ceae8a536b0", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Generators", "question": "During load shedding, the backup gas generator fails to pick up the factory load. How do you find the fault?", "key_points": ["Check the changeover or ATS and its control signals", "Check the generator start: battery, gas pressure and controls", "Check if the starting load is too big, such as many motors at once", "Fix it, then test the changeover under load with staggered motor starts"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "32efd8f1-78af-5825-8d22-4ec150aff09e", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Safety", "question": "You are asked to work on a live panel so production does not stop. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Refuse unsafe live work and explain the risk", "Plan a short shutdown with production", "If live work is truly needed: a permit, trained people and proper PPE", "Safety comes before output"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "f63ded69-473a-5028-acd4-293cb82d37cf", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Power factor", "question": "The factory's power factor dropped after new machines were added. How do you fix it?", "key_points": ["Measure power factor and harmonics with a power analyser", "Check that the capacitor bank and its controller are working", "Add capacitance in steps, with detuned reactors if harmonics are high", "Check the result on the meter and the next bill"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "76959380-e51d-511f-90fe-6adbaba65348", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Transformers", "question": "A distribution transformer is overheating in summer. What do you check?", "key_points": ["Load against rating, including unbalance between phases", "Oil level, oil condition and cooling", "Loose connections and the tap position", "Plan load shifting or a bigger transformer"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "1332a6a1-d3aa-57ed-925d-b56ef2b5c5e9", "role": "electrical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Protection", "question": "A factory wants to add rooftop solar connected to the grid. What do you need to think about?", "key_points": ["Roof strength, shading and the factory's daytime load", "Protection: anti-islanding, earthing and surge protection", "Follow the current net metering guidelines and get the utility's approval", "Panels stay live in daylight, so plan safe isolation for maintenance"], "source_url": "https://sreda.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "fa3be91d-3b06-517d-9bf5-46d223ea69d6", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Mobile network basics", "question": "In simple terms, what is the difference between 2G, 3G, 4G and 5G?", "key_points": ["Each generation adds speed and capacity", "2G: voice and SMS; 3G: mobile internet; 4G: fast mobile data; 5G: more speed, less delay", "Older networks often stay on for voice and older phones"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "384b0f98-a3dd-5f3e-a7b4-d383477b1eeb", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Mobile network basics", "question": "What is a base station, and what are its main parts?", "key_points": ["The site that links phones to the network by radio", "Antennas, radio units, a baseband unit and a transmission link", "A power system: grid, rectifiers, batteries and often a generator", "A tower or rooftop to hold the antennas"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "3ba4f70a-f7bf-58b3-873d-0bccff23747e", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Radio and KPIs", "question": "What is handover, and why does it sometimes fail?", "key_points": ["Passing a call or data session from one cell to the next as the user moves", "Fails with poor coverage, wrong neighbour lists or overloaded cells", "Shows up as dropped calls in the KPIs"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "b5e05252-0bbb-5dc1-99f7-d59877b67120", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Transmission", "question": "How does traffic get from a cell site to the core network?", "key_points": ["Through microwave links or optical fibre", "Fibre carries more; microwave is quicker to set up where there is no fibre", "Aggregation points collect traffic from many sites"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "2e193c05-680e-5397-a4ac-b530ac7bbd9e", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Safety", "question": "What safety steps must you follow before climbing a tower?", "key_points": ["Training and fitness for work at height", "Full body harness, helmet and a double lanyard, always tied off", "Checks the weather: no climbing in storms or strong wind", "A work permit and a partner on the ground"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "1fa6b3f5-17bb-5bd7-ba76-55c490f97fea", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Radio and KPIs", "question": "Name some key KPIs for a mobile network and what each one tells you.", "key_points": ["Call setup success rate: can users connect", "Call drop rate: do calls stay connected", "Data speed and latency: how fast data moves", "Availability: how much of the time sites are working"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "b0cc11e8-7333-57d2-a1cb-d7b8b0f71c7d", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Site power", "question": "A site keeps going down during load shedding. How do you find the cause?", "key_points": ["Reads the power logs: grid off, generator start, battery voltage", "Batteries may be old and not hold charge for long enough", "The generator may fail to start, run out of fuel or have a faulty switch", "Fixes the cause and plans maintenance or a battery change"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "60b12e90-679e-500d-8f7d-419c7b67c63c", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Field work", "question": "Customers in a rural union say their calls drop often. How would you investigate?", "key_points": ["Checks KPIs and alarms for the sites that serve the area", "Does a drive test to measure signal and quality", "Looks for coverage gaps, interference or wrong neighbour settings", "Suggests fixes: antenna tilt, power settings, or a new site"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "0b0507df-f7f5-5824-bb53-2b3218c1ffce", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Transmission", "question": "A microwave link fails whenever it rains heavily. Why, and what can you do?", "key_points": ["Heavy rain weakens high-frequency signals", "Checks the link budget and the fade margin", "Options: a lower frequency, larger antennas, a shorter hop, or a fibre backup", "Plans for it, because monsoon months make it common"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "5e750db5-e306-53b7-96e3-8cd39d373aa4", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Regulation", "question": "What does BTRC do, and why does it matter to a telecom engineer?", "key_points": ["BTRC is the telecom regulator: it issues licences and assigns spectrum", "It sets quality of service rules and checks operators against them", "Tower sharing and nationwide fibre networks also need licences", "Check BTRC's current rules before any site or frequency decision"], "source_url": "https://btrc.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "8b72ed82-1966-5e2b-8413-82b11d278fd3", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Core network", "question": "What does the core network do, and what happens to users if part of it fails?", "key_points": ["Connects calls, manages subscribers and routes data to the internet", "Checks who users are and what services they can use", "A core failure can hit a whole region, not just one site", "Redundancy and fast failover limit the damage"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "bfd4cb1d-26d3-55f9-8d8b-1c79bbd63fb1", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Safety", "question": "A teammate wants to climb a tower in strong wind to finish a job before dark. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Stops the climb: safety comes before targets", "Explains the risk and agrees a new time", "Tells the supervisor and records why the work was delayed", "Makes sure the site is safe to leave"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "6bea6c9a-df8c-5e8e-8289-520ccd6e7b0a", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Site power", "question": "Fuel cost and diesel theft are rising at your sites. How would you cut generator use?", "key_points": ["Keeps batteries healthy so they cover more of each outage", "Uses hybrid or solar power where it fits", "Monitors fuel levels and generator run hours remotely", "Checks reports for sites that use too much fuel"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "3b256a45-a249-57a7-9ec0-203dfd842102", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Radio and KPIs", "question": "After a new site goes live, call drops in the area rise. How do you find out why?", "key_points": ["Checks neighbour lists and handover settings for the new site", "Looks for interference or overlapping coverage", "Checks antenna direction and tilt against the plan", "Compares KPIs before and after, and changes one thing at a time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "50666f9e-e23e-5bdf-855c-132f2af5190a", "role": "telecommunications-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Field work", "question": "You must restore a down site in a flooded area during the monsoon. How do you plan the trip?", "key_points": ["Checks access, weather and safety before leaving", "Carries spares, tools and fuel based on the alarms", "Stays in contact with the NOC and a teammate", "Takes no risks with floodwater or live power"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "9fc2e2af-5356-5ee6-9a6e-3fa79de7a958", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Maintenance", "question": "What is the difference between preventive and breakdown maintenance?", "key_points": ["Breakdown maintenance: fix it after it fails", "Preventive maintenance: planned service so it does not fail", "Predictive maintenance uses data such as vibration or temperature", "Preventive work costs less over time for critical machines"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "290c17d8-889c-55c7-a9f8-88e26b2255f2", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Pumps", "question": "What is cavitation in a pump, and how do you prevent it?", "key_points": ["Vapour bubbles form when suction pressure is too low, then collapse", "It causes noise, vibration and damage to the impeller", "Keep the available NPSH above the pump's required NPSH", "Keep suction lines short, clean and wide enough"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "5534822e-9bd1-52d2-b24d-d282a76c0a4a", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Materials", "question": "What is the difference between stress and strain?", "key_points": ["Stress: force divided by area", "Strain: change in length divided by the original length", "In the elastic range, stress divided by strain is Young's modulus", "Used to check whether a part can carry its load"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "3c042432-8df1-57f5-9161-53c4b6f52087", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Drawings and CAD", "question": "What is a tolerance on a drawing, and why does it matter?", "key_points": ["The allowed variation in a dimension", "Parts must fit and work together", "Tighter tolerances cost more to make", "Check the fit needed, such as clearance or interference"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "0dc2eeb4-ce5d-5a25-a4da-889f67e0bae8", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Safety", "question": "What safety checks do you do before starting maintenance on a machine?", "key_points": ["Isolate and lock out power, air and other energy", "Release stored pressure and let hot parts cool", "Use the right PPE and tools", "Get a work permit where one is needed"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "99251cfc-3d88-5d92-87c7-7189f67bb56d", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Boilers and compressors", "question": "What safety devices does a steam boiler have, and why are they important?", "key_points": ["Safety valves, a pressure gauge and a water level gauge", "A low-water cut-off and alarms", "They prevent explosions from too much pressure or too little water", "Test them on schedule and record the results"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "6369c775-6964-5536-b527-ce6ceadfffd7", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Generators", "question": "How do you maintain a gas generator in a factory?", "key_points": ["Follow the maker's service schedule by running hours", "Change oil, filters and spark plugs, and check cooling", "Watch gas pressure, alarms and exhaust temperature", "Keep logs and look for trends"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "1c525e0e-7e32-57a3-8d83-055222248327", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "HVAC", "question": "How would you size the air conditioning for an office in Dhaka?", "key_points": ["Work out the cooling load: room size, people, lights, equipment and sun", "Allow for heat and high humidity", "Choose the system type: split, VRF or chiller", "Include ventilation and fresh air"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "ff0447ea-197b-5858-a730-222154ab933e", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Boilers and compressors", "question": "A compressed air system cannot keep up with demand. What do you check?", "key_points": ["Leaks, which waste a lot of air", "Filters, dryers and pressure settings", "Whether demand has grown or air is being misused", "A better controller or another compressor"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "74849dad-4c57-5139-aafa-2a6c3f35eb9e", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Maintenance", "question": "Imported spare parts take weeks to arrive. How do you avoid long breakdowns?", "key_points": ["List the critical spares for key machines", "Keep a minimum stock and reorder early", "Find local suppliers, or make some parts locally", "Plan maintenance before parts fail"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "78464019-6120-5f33-b8ff-6553ce320ff5", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Pumps", "question": "A pump is vibrating badly and making noise. How do you find the cause?", "key_points": ["Check alignment, bearings and mounting", "Check for cavitation or a blocked suction", "Measure vibration and compare it with past readings", "Fix the root cause, not only the symptom"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "9d183d69-dedf-50ab-8654-2998c46354a7", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Generators", "question": "Gas pressure in your area drops at peak hours and the gas generators trip. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Record pressure and trips to find the pattern", "Talk to the gas supplier about the problem", "Run only critical loads when pressure is low", "Consider a backup fuel, such as diesel, and its storage"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "373de5a6-f1cf-5cfc-9c56-ff4d3d5c055a", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Boilers and compressors", "question": "Your factory's boiler inspection is next month. How do you prepare?", "key_points": ["Boilers must be registered with and certified by the Office of the Chief Inspector of Boilers", "Check logs, water treatment records and past inspection reports", "Test safety valves and controls, and fix leaks before the visit", "Make sure operators are trained and know the emergency steps"], "source_url": "https://boiler.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "a143ea27-5407-5982-b1dd-033a9f6743a7", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "HVAC", "question": "Workers say the factory floor is too hot in summer. What could you do?", "key_points": ["Measure temperature and humidity at different points", "Improve ventilation with exhaust fans or evaporative cooling pads", "Reduce heat coming in: roof insulation or reflective coating", "Compare the cost and benefit of each option"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "969b6361-ec02-5d52-b94f-d9621c24bd3e", "role": "mechanical-engineer", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Materials", "question": "A shaft keeps breaking in the same place. How do you investigate?", "key_points": ["Look at the fracture surface for fatigue marks or a sudden break", "Check the design for stress points such as keyways or sharp corners", "Check the material, heat treatment and real loads", "Change the design or material, then test it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "9d36c3b8-1abc-5a13-bdcf-da9b99c4d36e", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Project cycle", "question": "What are the main stages of a development project?", "key_points": ["Needs assessment and design", "Approval and detailed planning", "Implementation and monitoring", "Evaluation, learning and close-out"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "27762731-605b-5540-a518-45e3501e5bfa", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Logframe", "question": "What is a logframe, and what are its main parts?", "key_points": ["A table linking activities to outputs, outcomes and the goal", "Each level has indicators and means of verification", "Assumptions: what must hold true outside the project", "Used to plan, monitor and report"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "916c2e55-599f-5a28-bde5-9078a22ae221", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Community work", "question": "How would you introduce a new project to a community in a village?", "key_points": ["Meet local leaders and the union parishad first, with respect", "Explain the project in simple Bangla, including what it will not provide", "Listen to what people need and what worries them", "Agree how people can give feedback or complain"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "bad3c6a1-c527-51db-a0f1-2995cfd21ade", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Safeguarding", "question": "What does safeguarding mean in an NGO?", "key_points": ["Protecting the people we serve, especially children, from harm by staff or partners", "A code of conduct and safe recruitment", "Clear, safe ways to report a concern", "Acting on every report and protecting the person who reports"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "4b4ee62e-0597-5b2a-8189-dcd320ed660b", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Donor reporting", "question": "What makes a good progress report to a donor?", "key_points": ["Progress against the plan and indicators, with numbers", "Honest about delays and problems, with actions", "Short examples from the field, shared with consent", "Sent on time in the donor's format"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "8212a948-cff4-5571-868b-c001798b3f3f", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Budgets", "question": "Halfway through the year, one budget line is overspent and another is underspent. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Find out why: a wrong plan, price changes or delays", "Check the donor's rules on moving money between lines", "Get approval before moving funds where it is needed", "Update the plan and tell your manager"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "29b85708-501a-5a92-8be5-7848c232a787", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Field logistics", "question": "You are organising a two-day training for 50 farmers in an upazila. What do you plan?", "key_points": ["A venue and dates that suit farm work and the season", "Transport, food, materials and allowances under the policy", "Simple Bangla sessions with practical demonstrations", "Attendance sheets and feedback for reporting"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "0c91de39-bf84-5214-a4d7-e324c6fe9acc", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Partners", "question": "A local partner organisation is late with its reports and spending. How do you handle it?", "key_points": ["Meet them to find the cause: staff, cash flow or skills", "Agree a clear plan with support and dates", "Check records on a field visit", "Escalate under the partner agreement if it continues"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "a1fe6ddb-ad72-59ac-8c84-e7a043a68ca8", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Project cycle", "question": "A foreign-funded project is ready to start. What government approval does it need, and how do you plan for it?", "key_points": ["NGOs need the NGO Affairs Bureau's approval before using foreign funds for a project", "The proposal goes to the Bureau on its set form", "Build approval time into the plan before activities start", "Check the current forms and rules on the Bureau's website"], "source_url": "https://ngoab.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "695ba08b-bb5b-54cb-aa7d-61aa0c06a19c", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Community work", "question": "How would you make sure women and the poorest households can take part in a project?", "key_points": ["Hold meetings at times and places that suit them", "Use women staff and separate sessions where needed", "Remove costs and other barriers to joining", "Track who takes part and adjust"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "99fc10e3-5553-58a0-9cb2-603aded9f68e", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Field logistics", "question": "A cyclone warning is issued for your project area. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Follow the emergency plan and keep staff safe", "Share warnings and support evacuation with local authorities", "Protect records, cash and supplies", "Prepare a quick needs assessment for after the storm"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "c26d2f65-2520-587b-8f40-7c80c028884e", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Safeguarding", "question": "A villager tells you a staff member asked for money to put their name on a support list. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Thank them, listen and write down the facts", "Report it at once through the complaint or whistleblowing channel", "Keep the person's identity safe", "Do not investigate alone or confront the staff member"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "228a7ae3-751b-5dfc-99c0-5b60eafe6d7e", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Donor reporting", "question": "Your project will miss a target the donor cares about. How do you report it?", "key_points": ["Tell the donor early, not in the final report", "Explain the reason with evidence", "Propose a realistic revised plan", "Show what was achieved and learned"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "32eb2ffc-888b-5727-9edc-76a76a85023a", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Partners", "question": "Many organisations are running a humanitarian response in the same area. How do you avoid duplication?", "key_points": ["Join the coordination meetings and share your plans", "Use shared beneficiary lists or maps where they exist", "Agree who does what, and where", "Share data carefully and protect personal information"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "112a28eb-db3a-5e24-8984-1b5d2e89c83a", "role": "development-programme-associate", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Budgets", "question": "Loan repayments in a microfinance programme are falling after a flood. What do you look at, and whose rules apply?", "key_points": ["Find which areas and borrowers are affected, and why", "Options under policy: rescheduling, a grace period or emergency support", "Balance borrowers' welfare with the programme's health", "Microfinance NGOs are licensed by the Microcredit Regulatory Authority and follow its rules"], "source_url": "https://mra.gov.bd/", "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "f6525160-d022-5792-92b9-9154f978e7e7", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Indicators", "question": "What is the difference between an output indicator and an outcome indicator?", "key_points": ["Output: what the project delivers, such as people trained", "Outcome: the change that follows, such as better farming practice", "Outcomes matter more but are harder to measure", "Gives an example from a real project"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "efef617c-59f4-51a3-882d-73189cf4d9f6", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Indicators", "question": "What makes a good indicator?", "key_points": ["SMART: specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound", "A clear definition so everyone counts it the same way", "Data you can actually collect at a fair cost", "Linked to the logframe"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "792cda85-2745-5d44-9eaf-8d1ad8f321af", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Baseline and endline", "question": "What is a baseline survey, and why is it needed?", "key_points": ["Data collected before the project starts", "Shows the starting point", "Lets you measure change at the endline", "Uses the same questions and methods both times"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "93ee559c-87da-5d1d-9211-0d2dd5bbe941", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Data tools", "question": "Have you used KoboToolbox or ODK? How does mobile data collection work?", "key_points": ["A form is built and loaded onto phones or tablets", "Enumerators collect data offline and upload when they have a signal", "Built-in checks reduce errors", "Data reaches a server where it can be reviewed quickly"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "63d78fad-3ee4-5b0d-b83f-0ab503ab3f9f", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Reporting", "question": "What do you do on a monitoring visit to a project site?", "key_points": ["Check activities against the plan", "Talk to participants and staff", "Check records and data", "Write a short visit report with actions"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "dff5cd45-411c-517e-94f8-75d44d5e9177", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Data cleaning", "question": "You receive survey data with duplicates, missing values and impossible answers. How do you clean it?", "key_points": ["Keep the raw file unchanged and work on a copy", "Find duplicates, out-of-range values and wrong skips", "Check with the field team where possible", "Record every change in a cleaning log"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "00f69969-b1a7-5948-bf60-6cc0f2dbcbc6", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Sampling", "question": "How would you choose households for an endline survey in 20 villages?", "key_points": ["Use the same sampling method as the baseline", "Choose randomly from a household list", "Plan for households that moved or refuse", "Work out the sample size needed"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "f028ea93-78d4-5684-ad7b-178fc76ca0cc", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Data tools", "question": "Your survey form will be used in Bangla by enumerators. How do you prepare and test it?", "key_points": ["Translate the questions and have them translated back", "Add skip logic and checks in the form", "Pre-test it in a nearby village", "Fix problems and train the enumerators"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "3515b4f3-82c5-5b1a-8bd2-6ae570c04169", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Consent", "question": "How do you collect data from children or other vulnerable people ethically?", "key_points": ["Get a parent's or guardian's consent and the child's own agreement", "Explain in simple words and make it voluntary", "Protect privacy and store data safely", "Have a referral plan if someone needs help"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "5adfe188-3c00-5144-9b2b-c9361ec497f1", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Analysis", "question": "How would you show whether a training improved farmers' yields?", "key_points": ["Compare yields before and after for trained farmers", "Compare with similar farmers who were not trained", "Allow for weather and other changes", "Show the result clearly, with its limits"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "578b06c4-8da8-530b-917d-7f33b245e33e", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Baseline and endline", "question": "The endline shows no change from the baseline, but staff say the project worked. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Check data quality and whether the indicators measure the right change", "Look at sub-groups: some may have improved", "Gather stories and other qualitative evidence", "Report honestly, with possible reasons"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "64fd39c6-1c43-5fe1-bcc1-80450d2c3fd7", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Data cleaning", "question": "You suspect an enumerator made up some interviews. How do you check?", "key_points": ["Check GPS points, timestamps and interview length", "Look for repeated answer patterns", "Back-check some households by phone or a visit", "Remove false data and report it"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "c6aadbbb-91ad-5ce1-a8fa-c1dc4926b573", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Reporting", "question": "A donor wants a monthly dashboard of project results. How would you set it up?", "key_points": ["Agree a small set of key indicators", "Set up one data flow from the field to one database", "Build a simple dashboard in Excel or Power BI", "Check the data before sharing and add short notes"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "6fa28938-f622-57ff-aa1e-64240f4d4af0", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Sampling", "question": "Flooding stops field teams reaching some sampled villages. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Keep teams safe and postpone where needed", "Replace villages by a fair rule decided in advance, and record it", "Consider a phone survey for those households", "Explain the change in the report"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "a0924e07-67b6-5d9c-99ac-74063fa67267", "role": "monitoring-and-evaluation-assistant", "kind": "role", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Analysis", "question": "How would you use BBS data alongside your project data?", "key_points": ["Use BBS figures as a benchmark for the area", "Check that definitions and years match", "Explain any differences", "Cite the source and the year"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "e1b0dcf3-e7ff-570c-a0fb-56421f8c4672", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Intro", "question": "Tell me about yourself.", "key_points": ["Present, then past, then why this role", "One real example that proves a strength", "Under two minutes, not your whole life story"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 1},
{"id": "50a78f3d-d069-517c-9e49-9332e5f74740", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Motivation", "question": "Why do you want this job, and why here?", "key_points": ["Names something specific about this employer's work, from real research", "Links the role to your skills and what you want to learn", "Salary or 'any job will do' is not the main reason"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 2},
{"id": "0ebf6fcd-96c9-51f0-a201-65cb54b61882", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Self-awareness", "question": "What are you good at, and what are you working on?", "key_points": ["One strength, with proof from a real example", "One real weakness, not a strength in disguise", "What you are doing about it now, and the progress so far"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 3},
{"id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Conflict", "question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 4},
{"id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Ownership", "question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 5},
{"id": "aa35c31c-7808-5254-b523-d149fe28f7df", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Failure", "question": "Tell me about a deadline you missed. What did you do about it?", "key_points": ["Owns the miss without blaming others", "Told people early and agreed a new plan", "Names what you changed so it does not happen again"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 6},
{"id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Humility", "question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 7},
{"id": "09608131-a474-5c13-a4f5-78740b907102", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Prioritising", "question": "You have three tasks and time for one. How do you choose, and who do you tell?", "key_points": ["Compares impact, urgency and who is waiting", "Checks with the manager when the priority is not clear", "Tells the people whose work will wait, with a new time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 8},
{"id": "96352762-2fdd-5b20-b475-63c043c2616a", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Direction", "question": "Where do you want to be in five years, and what are you doing about it this month?", "key_points": ["A realistic direction linked to this field", "Concrete steps you are taking this month", "Shows this job is part of the plan, not a short stop"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 9},
{"id": "b5005df4-cb6d-5dfc-ba93-3e4f769f273d", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "HR round", "question": "When could you join if we offered you the job?", "key_points": ["Gives a clear date or notice period", "Mentions anything fixed, such as a final exam or result date", "Does not promise a date you cannot keep"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 10},
{"id": "eed09620-a598-51e2-9461-99412d8903e2", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "HR round", "question": "What salary do you expect, in taka, and how did you reach that figure?", "key_points": ["Gives a monthly range in taka, not 'anything is fine'", "Explains the basis: the usual rate for this role, your skills, living costs", "Stays open to the full package, not only the basic salary", "Calm and polite, without underselling yourself"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 11},
{"id": "177435cf-1246-580c-be87-77fbd8f77551", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Teamwork", "question": "Tell me about a group project at university. What was your part?", "key_points": ["Names your own part clearly", "One concrete result or piece of work you produced", "How the group shared work and solved a problem", "What you would do differently next time"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 12},
{"id": "24f0a64b-91be-594a-8d4d-6af8b428e57f", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Learning", "question": "Tell me about something you taught yourself outside class.", "key_points": ["Names the skill and why you chose it", "How you learned it: a course, practice, a mentor, videos", "Shows proof: something you made or used it for"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 13},
{"id": "ef9555be-a820-5619-af6d-f0c95087e9ab", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "category": "Interests", "question": "What do you do outside study or work, and what has it taught you?", "key_points": ["One real interest, told briefly and honestly", "A skill it built, such as discipline, patience or teamwork", "Keeps it short and links it to work if it fits"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 14},
{"id": "00132b23-dba4-56cf-8b9e-4877047a8e19", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "HR round", "question": "This job may mean working outside Dhaka, in a factory or in the field. How do you feel about that?", "key_points": ["Gives an honest answer, not just a quick yes", "Names any real limit and how you would manage it", "Shows interest in what you would learn on site"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 15},
{"id": "4c33060f-f9f9-5bcf-a2cf-217394aa8088", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "HR round", "question": "Why should we choose you over the other graduates who applied?", "key_points": ["Two or three strengths tied to this role", "Proof for each one: a project, a job, a result", "Does not run other candidates down", "Ends with what you would bring in the first months"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 16},
{"id": "1a207c86-29bf-5664-b6b7-ec4a121aec08", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Customer handling", "question": "A customer or buyer calls you, angry, about a problem you did not cause. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Listens without interrupting and stays calm", "Says sorry for the trouble without blaming a colleague", "Finds the facts and gives a clear next step and a time", "Calls back when you said you would"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 17},
{"id": "bd2a92de-91a0-5146-93c5-6ebb063b2dad", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Communication", "question": "Your manager gives instructions only by voice, and you have made mistakes from misunderstanding. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Repeats the instruction back to check you understood", "Sends a short written note or message afterwards to confirm", "Raises it politely, without blaming the manager", "Shows the result: fewer mistakes"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 18},
{"id": "02b5c620-5ac6-536b-9aba-56645e6fcd44", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "category": "Adaptability", "question": "You are sent for two weeks of field work in a remote upazila with a weak network. How do you prepare and keep your work on track?", "key_points": ["Plans ahead: offline copies of forms, a power bank, local contacts", "Agrees with the manager how and when you will report", "Works respectfully with local people and staff", "Keeps daily notes so nothing is lost"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 19},
{"id": "b4f9f1a7-966d-5904-9cf4-0bde6296383c", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "HR round", "question": "Do you plan to study abroad or sit a government job exam in the next two years? Please be honest.", "key_points": ["Gives an honest answer; a vague one sounds worse", "If yes, explains how you would still deliver while you are here", "Names what this job would teach you either way", "Does not make promises you cannot keep"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 20},
{"id": "ca2dc09d-5978-5db1-a210-ccda54df5656", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Integrity", "question": "Someone you know from your area or university asks you to bend a rule at work for them. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Says no politely and explains the rule", "Offers the proper way to get what they need", "Tells your manager if the pressure continues", "Treats them the same as anyone else"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 21},
{"id": "7226473e-59c5-5a7d-a297-058add58b0b4", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Pressure", "question": "There is a power cut on the day a big piece of work is due, and the generator fails too. What do you do?", "key_points": ["Tells the manager or client early: what is done and what is left", "Uses what still works: a laptop battery, mobile data, another office", "Agrees a new time or a smaller first delivery", "Afterwards sets up a backup, such as saving online and charging devices"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 22},
{"id": "e6791706-8f81-5dbb-a14b-0fdf6882097d", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Feedback", "question": "Tell me about a time you got hard feedback. What did you change afterwards?", "key_points": ["Names the feedback honestly", "How you took it without arguing or giving excuses", "One concrete change and what it led to"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 23},
{"id": "474d5f9e-9677-5e82-b4c0-244caad006e3", "role": null, "kind": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "category": "Leadership", "question": "Tell me about a time you got people to act when you had no authority over them.", "key_points": ["Explains the goal and why it mattered to them, not only to you", "How you listened and shared the work fairly", "What you did when someone did not follow through", "The result, and what you learned about leading"], "source_url": null, "sort_order": 24}
]$pool$::jsonb)
  as q(id uuid, role text, kind text, difficulty difficulty_level, category text,
       question text, key_points jsonb, source_url text, sort_order int);

insert into public.interview_pool_questions
  (id, role_slug, kind, difficulty, category, question, key_points, source_url,
   sort_order, is_active)
select id, role, kind, difficulty, category, question, key_points, source_url,
       sort_order, true
  from pool_seed_questions
on conflict (id) do update set
  role_slug = excluded.role_slug, kind = excluded.kind, difficulty = excluded.difficulty,
  category = excluded.category, question = excluded.question,
  key_points = excluded.key_points, source_url = excluded.source_url,
  sort_order = excluded.sort_order, is_active = true;

update public.interview_pool_questions set is_active = false
 where is_active and id not in (select id from pool_seed_questions);

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------- sets
-- The fixed sets old app builds read through the interview function: the
-- same item shape as 0069 plus key_points and pool_id, which they ignore.
insert into public.interview_question_bank (role_slug, session_type, difficulty, questions, source)
select s.role, s.session_type, s.difficulty, s.questions, 'seed'
  from jsonb_to_recordset($sets$[
{"role": "industrial-engineer", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about yourself.", "category": "Intro", "key_points": ["Present, then past, then why this role", "One real example that proves a strength", "Under two minutes, not your whole life story"], "pool_id": "e1b0dcf3-e7ff-570c-a0fb-56421f8c4672"}, {"question": "Why do you want this job, and why here?", "category": "Motivation", "key_points": ["Names something specific about this employer's work, from real research", "Links the role to your skills and what you want to learn", "Salary or 'any job will do' is not the main reason"], "pool_id": "50a78f3d-d069-517c-9e49-9332e5f74740"}, {"question": "What are you good at, and what are you working on?", "category": "Self-awareness", "key_points": ["One strength, with proof from a real example", "One real weakness, not a strength in disguise", "What you are doing about it now, and the progress so far"], "pool_id": "0ebf6fcd-96c9-51f0-a201-65cb54b61882"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}]},
{"role": "industrial-engineer", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about yourself.", "category": "Intro", "key_points": ["Present, then past, then why this role", "One real example that proves a strength", "Under two minutes, not your whole life story"], "pool_id": "e1b0dcf3-e7ff-570c-a0fb-56421f8c4672"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}, {"question": "Tell me about a deadline you missed. What did you do about it?", "category": "Failure", "key_points": ["Owns the miss without blaming others", "Told people early and agreed a new plan", "Names what you changed so it does not happen again"], "pool_id": "aa35c31c-7808-5254-b523-d149fe28f7df"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "category": "Humility", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "pool_id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322"}]},
{"role": "industrial-engineer", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "category": "Humility", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "pool_id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322"}, {"question": "You have three tasks and time for one. How do you choose, and who do you tell?", "category": "Prioritising", "key_points": ["Compares impact, urgency and who is waiting", "Checks with the manager when the priority is not clear", "Tells the people whose work will wait, with a new time"], "pool_id": "09608131-a474-5c13-a4f5-78740b907102"}, {"question": "Where do you want to be in five years, and what are you doing about it this month?", "category": "Direction", "key_points": ["A realistic direction linked to this field", "Concrete steps you are taking this month", "Shows this job is part of the plan, not a short stop"], "pool_id": "96352762-2fdd-5b20-b475-63c043c2616a"}]},
{"role": "industrial-engineer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "What is SMV, and how is it used in a garment factory?", "category": "Time study and SMV", "key_points": ["Standard minute value: the time a trained operator needs for one operation, with allowances", "The SMV of all operations added together gives the garment SMV", "Used for costing, daily targets, line planning and efficiency"], "pool_id": "2de95c76-9af1-5da4-b079-cea46700e27e"}, {"question": "How do you do a time study for one sewing operation?", "category": "Time study and SMV", "key_points": ["Break the operation into clear elements", "Time a trained operator over several cycles, with a stopwatch or video", "Rate the operator's pace and add allowances for fatigue and delays", "Tell the operator what you are doing and why"], "pool_id": "46aa16cb-bfd4-5431-9cc1-8c4cdc92073d"}, {"question": "How do you calculate the efficiency of a sewing line?", "category": "Efficiency", "key_points": ["Efficiency is minutes produced divided by minutes attended", "Minutes produced: pieces made times the garment SMV", "Minutes attended: operators times working minutes", "Read it with quality: high output with high rework is not good"], "pool_id": "770acc12-1c1f-5371-8ef4-8c4533b5add0"}, {"question": "One operation on the line is a bottleneck. How do you find it and fix it?", "category": "Line balancing", "key_points": ["Look for work piling up in front of one operator, and check cycle times", "Compare its time with the line's target pitch time", "Fixes: split the operation, move a skilled or extra operator, add a helper or attachment", "Check the flow again after the change"], "pool_id": "e57148b0-7613-5835-9239-c8ed16d02170"}, {"question": "How do you work out how many pieces a line can make in a day on a new style?", "category": "Capacity planning", "key_points": ["Use the number of operators, working minutes, garment SMV and expected efficiency", "Daily target: operators times minutes times efficiency, divided by SMV", "Allow for the learning curve in the first days of a new style", "Agree the plan with production and planning"], "pool_id": "b2e7a0a2-5cd3-54ec-99b9-983a35ece934"}]},
{"role": "industrial-engineer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "What is SMV, and how is it used in a garment factory?", "category": "Time study and SMV", "key_points": ["Standard minute value: the time a trained operator needs for one operation, with allowances", "The SMV of all operations added together gives the garment SMV", "Used for costing, daily targets, line planning and efficiency"], "pool_id": "2de95c76-9af1-5da4-b079-cea46700e27e"}, {"question": "One operation on the line is a bottleneck. How do you find it and fix it?", "category": "Line balancing", "key_points": ["Look for work piling up in front of one operator, and check cycle times", "Compare its time with the line's target pitch time", "Fixes: split the operation, move a skilled or extra operator, add a helper or attachment", "Check the flow again after the change"], "pool_id": "e57148b0-7613-5835-9239-c8ed16d02170"}, {"question": "How do you work out how many pieces a line can make in a day on a new style?", "category": "Capacity planning", "key_points": ["Use the number of operators, working minutes, garment SMV and expected efficiency", "Daily target: operators times minutes times efficiency, divided by SMV", "Allow for the learning curve in the first days of a new style", "Agree the plan with production and planning"], "pool_id": "b2e7a0a2-5cd3-54ec-99b9-983a35ece934"}, {"question": "Rework on a line is high. How would you find the main causes?", "category": "Quality", "key_points": ["Collect defect data by operation and type, for example with a check sheet", "Use a Pareto chart to find the few defects that cause most rework", "Go to the line, watch the operation and talk to the operator and supervisor", "Fix the root cause: method, machine, training or material"], "pool_id": "8d7b2a32-9aaf-5efd-8b9e-10724d72f27a"}, {"question": "The production manager wants higher targets, but operators say the current target is already too hard. What do you do?", "category": "People", "key_points": ["Check the SMV and the method again with a fresh time study", "Look for real waste to remove before asking people to work faster", "Set targets that a trained operator can meet in normal hours", "Explain the numbers to both sides honestly"], "pool_id": "fb7fc688-6e2e-5ca5-9ce0-15f826400e41"}]},
{"role": "industrial-engineer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "hard", "questions": [{"question": "One operation on the line is a bottleneck. How do you find it and fix it?", "category": "Line balancing", "key_points": ["Look for work piling up in front of one operator, and check cycle times", "Compare its time with the line's target pitch time", "Fixes: split the operation, move a skilled or extra operator, add a helper or attachment", "Check the flow again after the change"], "pool_id": "e57148b0-7613-5835-9239-c8ed16d02170"}, {"question": "How do you work out how many pieces a line can make in a day on a new style?", "category": "Capacity planning", "key_points": ["Use the number of operators, working minutes, garment SMV and expected efficiency", "Daily target: operators times minutes times efficiency, divided by SMV", "Allow for the learning curve in the first days of a new style", "Agree the plan with production and planning"], "pool_id": "b2e7a0a2-5cd3-54ec-99b9-983a35ece934"}, {"question": "The production manager wants higher targets, but operators say the current target is already too hard. What do you do?", "category": "People", "key_points": ["Check the SMV and the method again with a fresh time study", "Look for real waste to remove before asking people to work faster", "Set targets that a trained operator can meet in normal hours", "Explain the numbers to both sides honestly"], "pool_id": "fb7fc688-6e2e-5ca5-9ce0-15f826400e41"}, {"question": "Efficiency on a line dropped this week. How do you find out why, and how do you report it?", "category": "Efficiency", "key_points": ["Check the inputs first: attendance, style changes, machine breakdowns, waiting for cut pieces", "Compare hourly output with targets to see when it fell", "Separate one-off causes from ones that keep happening", "Report a short summary with numbers: cause, effect and action"], "pool_id": "1c50dc87-1be3-5685-99f7-44cab448b310"}, {"question": "Planning wants a large order shipped in four weeks. How do you check if the factory can do it?", "category": "Capacity planning", "key_points": ["Minutes needed: order quantity times SMV", "Compare with the available minutes of lines that can make this style", "Include the learning curve, other orders, holidays and power cuts", "If short, give options: more lines, extra hours within the rules, an approved subcontractor"], "pool_id": "06eb3558-68a6-5d75-9b3d-5ba4770fbb5c"}]},
