{"role": "software-engineer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between an array and a linked list? When would you use each?", "category": "Data structures", "key_points": ["Array: items side by side in memory, fast to read by index", "Linked list: each item points to the next, easy to insert or remove", "Array for reading by position; linked list for many inserts in the middle", "Names the big O cost of reading and inserting for each"], "pool_id": "31274e90-5e57-5975-949b-f22397c640ab"}, {"question": "What does big O notation tell you? Explain O(n) and O(log n) with an example.", "category": "Algorithms", "key_points": ["How time or memory grows as the input grows", "O(n): one pass through a list, such as finding the largest number", "O(log n): the problem halves each step, such as binary search", "Explains it in plain words, not only symbols"], "pool_id": "e355ff47-9ae9-5b6d-b945-47c620a4c469"}, {"question": "Explain encapsulation, inheritance and polymorphism with a simple example.", "category": "OOP", "key_points": ["Encapsulation: hide data behind methods", "Inheritance: one class reuses and extends another", "Polymorphism: one interface, different behaviour", "Uses one small real example, such as different payment types"], "pool_id": "17c743b2-ca2a-5c4b-9d7f-7d4b2fadf3af"}, {"question": "How would you check whether a list has duplicate numbers? Give two ways and compare them.", "category": "Algorithms", "key_points": ["Compare every pair: simple, but O(n squared)", "Sort first, then compare neighbours: O(n log n)", "Use a hash set: O(n) time, but extra memory", "Talks through the trade-off out loud, as in a live coding round"], "pool_id": "e7838065-85ed-55e7-8f3f-d923e5ca9315"}, {"question": "Your solution works for small inputs but times out on large ones in an online judge. What do you do?", "category": "Debugging", "key_points": ["Works out the time complexity of the current solution", "Finds the slow part: nested loops or repeated work", "Picks a better approach: hashing, sorting, two pointers or caching", "Tests edge cases: empty input, one item, the largest input"], "pool_id": "0feb1309-d055-58a1-b098-41ab47d0a305"}]},
