{"role": "market-research-analyst", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about yourself.", "category": "Intro", "key_points": ["Present, then past, then why this role", "One real example that proves a strength", "Under two minutes, not your whole life story"], "pool_id": "e1b0dcf3-e7ff-570c-a0fb-56421f8c4672"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}, {"question": "Tell me about a deadline you missed. What did you do about it?", "category": "Failure", "key_points": ["Owns the miss without blaming others", "Told people early and agreed a new plan", "Names what you changed so it does not happen again"], "pool_id": "aa35c31c-7808-5254-b523-d149fe28f7df"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "category": "Humility", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "pool_id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322"}]},
{"role": "market-research-analyst", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "category": "Humility", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "pool_id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322"}, {"question": "You have three tasks and time for one. How do you choose, and who do you tell?", "category": "Prioritising", "key_points": ["Compares impact, urgency and who is waiting", "Checks with the manager when the priority is not clear", "Tells the people whose work will wait, with a new time"], "pool_id": "09608131-a474-5c13-a4f5-78740b907102"}, {"question": "Where do you want to be in five years, and what are you doing about it this month?", "category": "Direction", "key_points": ["A realistic direction linked to this field", "Concrete steps you are taking this month", "Shows this job is part of the plan, not a short stop"], "pool_id": "96352762-2fdd-5b20-b475-63c043c2616a"}]},
{"role": "market-research-analyst", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between primary and secondary research? Give an example of each.", "category": "Research design", "key_points": ["Primary: data you collect yourself, such as a survey or interviews", "Secondary: data others collected, such as BBS reports or industry studies", "Start with secondary research to learn what is already known", "Use primary research to fill the gap for your exact question"], "pool_id": "7d69c784-dafc-5c04-8318-e5bcac841960"}, {"question": "What is the difference between qualitative and quantitative research?", "category": "Research design", "key_points": ["Qualitative: why and how, from interviews and group discussions", "Quantitative: how many and how much, from surveys and data", "Qualitative work often comes first to shape the survey", "Good studies often use both"], "pool_id": "597a6ada-731a-5e63-bad8-dc1bd20ca59d"}, {"question": "Where would you look for secondary data on a market in Bangladesh, such as exports of one product?", "category": "Research design", "key_points": ["Official statistics, such as BBS and the Export Promotion Bureau", "International trade databases for the buying countries", "Industry associations, company reports and trade press", "Check the date, definition and source of every figure"], "pool_id": "a7c5a0ba-b27f-5029-82b1-168b42f04ee5"}, {"question": "You need to survey shops in both urban and rural areas of a division. How would you choose the sample?", "category": "Sampling", "key_points": ["Define the population and find or build a list of shops", "Split by urban and rural so both are covered", "Pick randomly within each group, often in clusters to save travel", "Set the sample size from the precision needed and the budget"], "pool_id": "15b71d48-7543-54f2-bc87-530ad504c703"}, {"question": "Your questionnaire is in English and the field team will ask it in Bangla. How do you make sure it means the same thing?", "category": "Questionnaires", "key_points": ["Translate it, then have another person translate it back", "Use everyday Bangla, with local words where needed", "Pre-test with a few real respondents and fix confusing questions", "Train enumerators on what each question means"], "pool_id": "819d4aba-6649-5362-b45f-f9ac62a62390"}]},
{"role": "market-research-analyst", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between primary and secondary research? Give an example of each.", "category": "Research design", "key_points": ["Primary: data you collect yourself, such as a survey or interviews", "Secondary: data others collected, such as BBS reports or industry studies", "Start with secondary research to learn what is already known", "Use primary research to fill the gap for your exact question"], "pool_id": "7d69c784-dafc-5c04-8318-e5bcac841960"}, {"question": "You need to survey shops in both urban and rural areas of a division. How would you choose the sample?", "category": "Sampling", "key_points": ["Define the population and find or build a list of shops", "Split by urban and rural so both are covered", "Pick randomly within each group, often in clusters to save travel", "Set the sample size from the precision needed and the budget"], "pool_id": "15b71d48-7543-54f2-bc87-530ad504c703"}, {"question": "Your questionnaire is in English and the field team will ask it in Bangla. How do you make sure it means the same thing?", "category": "Questionnaires", "key_points": ["Translate it, then have another person translate it back", "Use everyday Bangla, with local words where needed", "Pre-test with a few real respondents and fix confusing questions", "Train enumerators on what each question means"], "pool_id": "819d4aba-6649-5362-b45f-f9ac62a62390"}, {"question": "Halfway through a survey, one enumerator's interviews are much shorter than everyone else's. What do you do?", "category": "Field work", "key_points": ["Check the data: timing, GPS and repeated answer patterns", "Back-check some respondents by phone or a visit", "Talk to the enumerator, then retrain or replace them", "Redo or remove bad interviews and note it in the report"], "pool_id": "58503c92-3187-5fd0-8f27-41ea9188ec12"}, {"question": "A client wants to know if farmers will pay 