s", "The client has agreed it and the files are ready"], "pool_id": "7271ddea-7d3e-54cf-aac4-d96cb6515a6d"}]},
{"role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about yourself.", "category": "Intro", "key_points": ["Present, then past, then why this role", "One real example that proves a strength", "Under two minutes, not your whole life story"], "pool_id": "e1b0dcf3-e7ff-570c-a0fb-56421f8c4672"}, {"question": "Why do you want this job, and why here?", "category": "Motivation", "key_points": ["Names something specific about this employer's work, from real research", "Links the role to your skills and what you want to learn", "Salary or 'any job will do' is not the main reason"], "pool_id": "50a78f3d-d069-517c-9e49-9332e5f74740"}, {"question": "What are you good at, and what are you working on?", "category": "Self-awareness", "key_points": ["One strength, with proof from a real example", "One real weakness, not a strength in disguise", "What you are doing about it now, and the progress so far"], "pool_id": "0ebf6fcd-96c9-51f0-a201-65cb54b61882"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}]},
{"role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about yourself.", "category": "Intro", "key_points": ["Present, then past, then why this role", "One real example that proves a strength", "Under two minutes, not your whole life story"], "pool_id": "e1b0dcf3-e7ff-570c-a0fb-56421f8c4672"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}, {"question": "Tell me about a deadline you missed. What did you do about it?", "category": "Failure", "key_points": ["Owns the miss without blaming others", "Told people early and agreed a new plan", "Names what you changed so it does not happen again"], "pool_id": "aa35c31c-7808-5254-b523-d149fe28f7df"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "category": "Humility", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "pool_id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322"}]},
{"role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "session_type": "behavioural", "difficulty": "hard", "questions": [{"question": "Tell me about a time you disagreed with someone on a team. What happened in the end?", "category": "Conflict", "key_points": ["Sets the scene briefly: who, what and why you disagreed", "Shows you listened and argued with facts, not feelings", "Says what was decided, even if it was not your idea", "Ends with what you learned about working with people"], "pool_id": "e5e29a76-652f-5a74-8da5-e281b809f299"}, {"question": "Describe something you built or organised from nothing. What went wrong?", "category": "Ownership", "key_points": ["What you started, and why it was needed", "Your own actions, step by step, using 'I' and not only 'we'", "One thing that went wrong and how you fixed it", "The result, with a number if you have one"], "pool_id": "08842ffe-dce2-5d5a-8310-a2c70e5924f6"}, {"question": "Tell me about a time you were wrong and someone else was right.", "category": "Humility", "key_points": ["A real example where you changed your mind", "How you found out you were wrong", "Gives the other person credit", "What you do differently now"], "pool_id": "6ec25f15-aae6-5571-a5ad-907d036de322"}, {"question": "You have three tasks and time for one. How do you choose, and who do you tell?", "category": "Prioritising", "key_points": ["Compares impact, urgency and who is waiting", "Checks with the manager when the priority is not clear", "Tells the people whose work will wait, with a new time"], "pool_id": "09608131-a474-5c13-a4f5-78740b907102"}, {"question": "Where do you want to be in five years, and what are you doing about it this month?", "category": "Direction", "key_points": ["A realistic direction linked to this field", "Concrete steps you are taking this month", "Shows this job is part of the plan, not a short stop"], "pool_id": "96352762-2fdd-5b20-b475-63c043c2616a"}]},
{"role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between UI and UX?", "category": "Process", "key_points": ["UX: how the whole experience works and feels for the user", "UI: the screens, layout, type, colour and controls", "Both start from what the user is trying to do"], "pool_id": "7d878834-d8a6-5937-b878-3d25bc62ba75"}, {"question": "What is a wireframe, and why make one before a detailed design?", "category": "Wireframes", "key_points": ["A simple layout of a screen without the final visuals", "Fast to change, so ideas are tested cheaply", "Keeps the focus on structure and flow first"], "pool_id": "79821f9e-3ae4-5760-82ef-603206a39200"}, {"question": "How would you find out what users need before you design?", "category": "Research", "key_points": ["Talks to real users, or watches them use the current app", "Looks at data: support complaints, app reviews, analytics", "Writes down the main problems and goals", "Checks ideas with more than one or two people"], "pool_id": "5fa26222-7f2a-599a-b605-1c8e6910bf8c"}, {"question": "How would you run a usability test with five users and almost no budget?", "category": "Usability testing", "key_points": ["Picks a few key tasks for users to try", "Watches quietly and asks them to think aloud, without helping", "Notes where they hesitate or fail", "Fixes the biggest problems first and tests again"], "pool_id": "8eda6df2-e3c0-5e12-8774-858323d19330"}, {"question": "Bangla labels are often longer than the English ones. How do you design for both?", "category": "Localisation", "key_points": ["Leaves room for longer text and avoids fixed-width buttons", "Tests every screen with real Bangla text, not placeholder text", "Chooses a font that shows Bangla clearly at small sizes", "Lets text wrap without breaking the layout"], "pool_id": "4e857b35-2cbc-58ac-b079-b188d4491379"}]},
{"role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between UI and UX?", "category": "Process", "key_points": ["UX: how the whole experience works and feels for the user", "UI: the screens, layout, type, colour and controls", "Both start from what the user is trying to do"], "pool_id": "7d878834-d8a6-5937-b878-3d25bc62ba75"}, {"question": "How would you run a usability test with five users and almost no budget?", "category": "Usability testing", "key_points": ["Picks a few key tasks for users to try", "Watches quietly and asks them to think aloud, without helping", "Notes where they hesitate or fail", "Fixes the biggest problems first and tests again"], "pool_id": "8eda6df2-e3c0-5e12-8774-858323d19330"}, {"question": "Bangla labels are often longer than the English ones. How do you design for both?", "category": "Localisation", "key_points": ["Leaves room for longer text and avoids fixed-width buttons", "Tests every screen with real Bangla text, not placeholder text", "Chooses a font that shows Bangla clearly at small sizes", "Lets text wrap without breaking the layout"], "pool_id": "4e857b35-2cbc-58ac-b079-b188d4491379"}, {"question": "You are designing a wallet app for people using a smartphone for the first time. What would you do differently?", "category": "Research", "key_points": ["One main action per screen and very simple steps", "Icons with words, and Bangla first where users prefer it", "A clear check before money moves, and easy help or undo", "Tests with real users from that group, including people who read little"], "pool_id": "2ce09fc9-c849-56a3-a760-4e78decf8a37"}, {"question": "Your test shows users fail at a step the product manager loves. How do you handle it?", "category": "Usability testing", "key_points": ["Shows the evidence: clips, quotes, how many users failed", "Keeps the focus on the user's goal, not on who is right", "Offers one or two alternatives to test quickly", "Agrees how success will be measured"], "pool_id": "c070ced9-c730-5b7c-903b-11a33c2baedf"}]},
{"role": "ui-and-ux-designer", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "hard", "questions": [{"question": "How would you run a usability test with five users and almost no budget?", "category": "Usability testing", "key_points": ["Picks a few key tasks for users to try", "Watches quietly and asks them to think aloud, without helping", "Notes where they hesitate or fail", "Fixes the biggest problems first and tests again"], "pool_id": "8eda6df2-e3c0-5e12-8774-858323d19330"}, {"question": "Bangla labels are often longer than the English ones. How do you design for both?", "category": "Localisation", "key_points": ["Leaves room for longer text and avoids fixed-width buttons", "Tests every screen with real Bangla text, not placeholder text", "Chooses a font that shows Bangla clearly at small sizes", "Lets text wrap without breaking the layout"], "pool_id": "4e857b35-2cbc-58ac-b079-b188d4491379"}, {"question": "Your test shows users fail at a step the product manager loves. How do you handle it?", "category": "Usability testing", "key_points": ["Shows the evidence: clips, quotes, how many users failed", "Keeps the focus on the user's goal, not on who is right", "Offers one or two alternatives to test quickly", "Agrees how success will be measured"], "pool_id": "c070ced9-c730-5b7c-903b-11a33c2baedf"}, {"question": "You have one week to design a feature that normally takes a month. What do you cut, and what do you keep?", "category": "Process", "key_points": ["Keeps the core user task and the riskiest question", "Cuts polish and side features for a later version", "Reuses parts from the design system", "Tests the core flow quickly with a few users"], "pool_id": "1478476f-d97c-599d-a8e2-e28fd78cd0e2"}, {"question": "How would you make an app work for someone who uses a screen reader?", "category": "Accessibility", "key_points": ["Every control has a clear label", "A logical reading order and headings", "Colour is never the only way to show meaning", "Tests with the phone's screen reader turned on"], "pool_id": "cff38dba-44d9-5da1-b42b-44f25d80cb83"}]},
