{"role": "data-analyst", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between the mean and the median, and when does it matter?", "category": "Statistics", "key_points": ["Mean: the total divided by the count; median: the middle value", "Outliers pull the mean but barely move the median", "Use the median for skewed data such as salaries or house prices"], "pool_id": "98096681-5a2c-5c2c-8df5-d62fcaa134ff"}, {"question": "You are handed a spreadsheet of sales. What are the first three things you check?", "category": "Data quality", "key_points": ["What each column means, and whether the totals look sensible", "Missing values, duplicates and wrong data types", "The date range, and whether every branch or region is there", "What question the data must answer"], "pool_id": "0449557d-76a5-521a-b1f0-b77c59c6dbf3"}, {"question": "Explain what a JOIN does to somebody who has never written SQL.", "category": "SQL", "key_points": ["A JOIN puts rows from two tables together using a shared column", "Example: orders matched to customers by customer ID", "An inner join keeps only matches; a left join keeps every row of the first table"], "pool_id": "b154546f-3e96-5c85-842e-d2aa595a7878"}, {"question": "A number in your report looks wrong. Walk me through how you check it.", "category": "Data quality", "key_points": ["Recalculates it from the raw data, step by step", "Checks filters, joins and date ranges for mistakes", "Compares it with another source or last month's figure", "Says so openly if it was wrong, and corrects it"], "pool_id": "bf0b6132-1854-5182-b3d2-83a8344a6104"}, {"question": "How would you find out which of two versions of a page performs better?", "category": "Experiments", "key_points": ["An A/B test: users split at random between the two versions", "One main metric agreed before the test starts", "Runs long enough for enough users, and checks the result is not chance", "Watches for other changes running at the same time"], "pool_id": "c9567a13-c74d-57f7-8712-0c006a0ba4aa"}]},
{"role": "data-analyst", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "medium", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between the mean and the median, and when does it matter?", "category": "Statistics", "key_points": ["Mean: the total divided by the count; median: the middle value", "Outliers pull the mean but barely move the median", "Use the median for skewed data such as salaries or house prices"], "pool_id": "98096681-5a2c-5c2c-8df5-d62fcaa134ff"}, {"question": "A number in your report looks wrong. Walk me through how you check it.", "category": "Data quality", "key_points": ["Recalculates it from the raw data, step by step", "Checks filters, joins and date ranges for mistakes", "Compares it with another source or last month's figure", "Says so openly if it was wrong, and corrects it"], "pool_id": "bf0b6132-1854-5182-b3d2-83a8344a6104"}, {"question": "How would you find out which of two versions of a page performs better?", "category": "Experiments", "key_points": ["An A/B test: users split at random between the two versions", "One main metric agreed before the test starts", "Runs long enough for enough users, and checks the result is not chance", "Watches for other changes running at the same time"], "pool_id": "c9567a13-c74d-57f7-8712-0c006a0ba4aa"}, {"question": "Your dashboard shows a spike last Tuesday. How do you work out whether it is real?", "category": "Dashboards", "key_points": ["Checks for data problems first: duplicates, a broken feed, a changed definition", "Looks at the raw rows behind the spike", "Looks for a real cause: a campaign, a holiday, a sale", "Confirms with the team that owns the data"], "pool_id": "bc01d528-ef94-51c0-8691-2abede031a69"}, {"question": "A manager asks 'why did revenue drop?'. How do you turn that into an analysis?", "category": "Framing", "key_points": ["Asks how much, since when, and compared with what", "Splits revenue into parts: customers, orders, price, product, region", "Rules out data problems before business causes", "Ends with a short answer and a next step"], "pool_id": "6a899293-19a1-5abf-997e-60f951cd050f"}]},
{"role": "data-analyst", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "hard", "questions": [{"question": "A number in your report looks wrong. Walk me through how you check it.", "category": "Data quality", "key_points": ["Recalculates it from the raw data, step by step", "Checks filters, joins and date ranges for mistakes", "Compares it with another source or last month's figure", "Says so openly if it was wrong, and corrects it"], "pool_id": "bf0b6132-1854-5182-b3d2-83a8344a6104"}, {"question": "How would you find out which of two versions of a page performs better?", "category": "Experiments", "key_points": ["An A/B test: users split at random between the two versions", "One main metric agreed before the test starts", "Runs long enough for enough users, and checks the result is not chance", "Watches for other changes running at the same time"], "pool_id": "c9567a13-c74d-57f7-8712-0c006a0ba4aa"}, {"question": "A manager asks 'why did revenue drop?'. How do you turn that into an analysis?", "category": "Framing", "key_points": ["Asks how much, since when, and compared with what", "Splits revenue into parts: customers, orders, price, product, region", "Rules out data problems before business causes", "Ends with a short answer and a next step"], "pool_id": "6a899293-19a1-5abf-997e-60f951cd050f"}, {"question": "What is the difference between correlation and causation? Give an example from your own work.", "category": "Statistics", "key_points": ["Correlation: two things move together; causation: one makes the other happen", "A third factor can drive both, such as Eid raising both ad spend and sales", "Gives a real example from a project", "Only a controlled test can show cause"], "pool_id": "43d9f973-0674-5cd0-8333-ac6148bb57af"}, {"question": "A third of a column is missing. What are your options, and how do you choose?", "category": "Data quality", "key_points": ["Finds out why it is missing, and whether that is random", "Options: drop the rows, fill with a sensible value, or flag as missing", "The choice depends on how the column is used and how much it matters", "Records the choice and shows its effect on the results"], "pool_id": "a1d66077-c766-5f78-b1b9-21c40407f626"}]},
