{"role": "textile-production-associate", "session_type": "technical", "difficulty": "easy", "questions": [{"question": "What is the difference between knit and woven fabric? Name a garment made from each.", "category": "Fibre and yarn", "key_points": ["Knit is loops from one yarn and stretches; woven crosses two sets of yarn", "Knit: T-shirt, polo. Woven: shirt, trousers, denim", "Factories usually specialise in one or the other"], "pool_id": "d9799e77-63ee-5f8e-9765-0c67554f51d7"}, {"question": "What does yarn count mean, and which is finer: 30s or 40s cotton yarn?", "category": "Fibre and yarn", "key_points": ["Count tells you how fine or coarse the yarn is", "In the cotton count system, a higher number means a finer yarn", "40s is finer than 30s and gives a lighter, smoother fabric"], "pool_id": "1713b755-d4bd-5bd3-81f7-36288575582e"}, {"question": "What is the difference between single jersey, rib and interlock fabric?", "category": "Knitting", "key_points": ["Single jersey: one needle bed, light, curls at the edge, used for T-shirts", "Rib: two needle beds, stretches across, used for collars, cuffs and fitted tops", "Interlock: two layers knitted together, thicker and smooth on both sides"], "pool_id": "6862c61a-f38b-5d17-bfbe-06c3cce0f8db"}, {"question": "The shade of a dyed batch does not match the approved lab dip. What do you check?", "category": "Process control", "key_points": ["Recipe and weighing: the right dyes, amounts and liquor ratio", "Process: temperature, time, pH, salt and alkali dosing", "Fabric: the same yarn lot and the same pretreatment", "Decide with the lab whether to add dye to correct it or strip and re-dye"], "pool_id": "d1c45942-5a95-50b1-bded-42f90970a4eb"}, {"question": "What is a lab dip, and why must the buyer approve it before bulk dyeing?", "category": "Dyeing and finishing", "key_points": ["A small sample dyed to match the buyer's colour standard", "Checked in a light box under the buyer's chosen light sources", "Approval fixes the recipe so the bulk can match it", "Saves the cost of re-dyeing a whole batch"], "pool_id": "bc21d0d8-5477-5b30-a959-88d234e541ff"}]},
